/ PYZ pyinstaller | 0x0d0d0a.. pyc magic\n106\t #@~^ ..^#~@ = Script-Encoder (.vbe/.jse) -> .venv/bin/wshenc < f\n107\tSHEBANG/HEADER -> language:\n108\t #!..perl / use strict;  -> perl      #!..ruby / require / def..end / =begin -> ruby\n109\t #!..tclsh / set x \"v\" / proc -> tcl  x <- v / library( -> R          package main / := -> go\n110\t fn main / let mut / r#\"..\"# -> rust  val/fun + plugins{ -> kotlin(.kts)   pipeline{ stages{ / def x= -> groovy/Jenkinsfile\n111\t BEGIN{ / getline -> awk              target:\\n\\tcmd / $(shell -> make     FROM / RUN -> Dockerfile\n112\t on:/jobs:/runs-on: -> GH Actions     stages:/script: -> GitLab CI          - hosts:/tasks: -> ansible\n113\t resource \"x\" / provisioner \"local-exec\" -> terraform    Windows Registry Editor 5.00 -> .reg\n114\t [Version] Signature=\"$CHICAGO$\" -> .inf   [InternetShortcut] -> .url   [Shell] Command= -> .scf\n115\t <xsl:stylesheet + msxsl:script -> XSLT (msxsl/wmic)   <scriptlet> -> SCT   <job> -> WSF   <hta:application> -> HTA\n116\t <Project ..msbuild> + UsingTask -> MSBuild    Installer + [RunInstaller(true)] -> InstallUtil C#\n117\t Sub AutoOpen/Document_Open/Attribute VB_Name -> VBA   =EXEC(/=FORMULA( in a sheet -> XLM\n118\t instance of __EventFilter -> MOF        #r \"nuget: -> csx   let/printfn/|> -> fsx   Deno./Bun. -> deno/bun\n119\tPLAN FIRST (the lane's contract since D2):\n120\t grep raw AND utf-16-decoded text for HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V\\d+ / Codec_ / CODEC_ / HUNTRESS-CODEC / MATERIAL_ / descriptor\n121\t descriptor syntaxes to accept: `x = \"..\"` `x := \"..\"` `set x \"..\"`/`set x {..}` `x <- \"..\"` `X: &str = \"..\"`\n122\t   `DESCRIPTOR_X = \"..\"` (Ruby const) `descriptor_x: \"..\"` (YAML) `<HuntressDescriptor>..</..>` (XML) heredoc/block scalar\n123\t material may wrap across lines (`|` YAML block, `=begin`, `<# #>`, `\"\"\"`, `\\` continuation, `.`/`+`/`&`/`..` concat):\n124\t   join the literal pieces, strip whitespace/separators, THEN peel\n125\t peel by SHAPE, max 4 layers, accept only output starting `v=` (or `{` JSON): hex (any separators) | base64 std/urlsafe\n126\t   (also reversed text) | base32 [A-Z2-7=] | base85/ascii85 <~~> | gzip H4sI / zlib eJ eN eF | rot13 | %xx | \\xNN \\NNN \\ddd\n127\t   \\uXXXX \\u{..} | int lists (READ the radix from code) | UTF-16LE inside b64 (PS -enc: every 2nd byte 00)\n128\t copy plan values verbatim (role, attack, adapter, steps, profiles, next_language); never derive them from code\n129\tLAYERED OBFUSCATION -> standard tool (static, no network, no exec of behaviour):\n130\t PowerShell   .venv/bin/ps1 < f  (folds -f reorder, `ticks, 'a'+'b', [char]N, -join, -replace, .Invoke)\n131\t JS           webcrack f.js -o out/  (obfuscator.io arrays) | .venv/bin/js < f | node hctf/js_sandbox.js f (eval->capture)\n132\t VBA/VBS      .venv/bin/olevba --decode --deobf f | .venv/bin/vba < f.bas | pcodedmp f.doc (stomped p-code)\n133\t Batch        .venv/bin/bat < f  (emulates set/%x:~a,b%/%x:a=b%/^/delayed !x!; prints commands, runs nothing)\n134\t XLM          .venv/bin/xlmdeobf < f.xls      OneNote .venv/bin/xtone -l < f.one     CHM .venv/bin/xtchm -l < f.chm\n135\t LNK          .venv/bin/lnk < f.lnk           AutoIt  autoit-ripper x.exe out/ | .venv/bin/a3x < f\n136\t Python       swap exec/eval->print, run with python3 -I in an empty dir; marshal blob -> pycdc / xdis (match version)\n137\t compressed   .venv/bin/b64 < blob | .venv/bin/decompress   (gzip/zlib/raw deflate/lzma/bz2 auto)\n138\t PHP chains   apply the named functions innermost-first in Python (base64_decode, gzinflate=raw deflate, str_rot13, strrev)\n139\tNEVER: run the fixture's interpreter on the file (ruby/perl/php/tclsh/Rscript/make/go run/msbuild/pwsh -File);\n140\t `perl -MO=Deparse` and `make -n` still execute BEGIN/$(shell) -> strip first; apply XSLT; open URLs from the plan.\n141\tSYNTHETIC LABELS (if a new language brings code-shape questions): read accepted_values; compose `<keyword>_guard`,\n142\t `<keyword>_once`, `<keyword>_<action>`; branch label tables on contract run_for_time:false (D15 regime flip).\n143\tATT&CK when no attack= in plan: role table in lib.scripts.role_attack; host-language sub-ids T1059.001 PS .002 AppleScript\n144\t .003 cmd .004 unix shell .005 VB .006 python .007 JS .010 AutoHotKey/AutoIt .011 Lua; v=3 plans so far used parent T1059.\n145\t```\n146\t\n147\t## Readiness gaps\n148\t```json\n149\t[\n150\t  {\"id\": \"v3-peel-widen\", \"concept\": \"v=3 marker/descriptor peel beyond hex/base64/reverse\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n151\t   \"detail\": \"solve.py _v3_peel only tries hex, base64 and reversal (3 layers). A new tag (B32, Z64/GZ, XOR, ROT, A85, URL, UTF-16 b64) silently yields no plan for 44 ids. Fall back to lib.decode.peel (already does b32/b85/a85/zlib/gzip/bz2/lzma/rot/url) with accept=looks_like_plan, depth 4; carry over to the D16 solver template.\"},\n152\t  {\"id\": \"source-encoding-normalize\", \"concept\": \"UTF-16LE/BE, BOM, gzip'd or base64'd leaf before marker scan\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n153\t   \"detail\": \"V3_MARK, Codec_ regexes and descriptor scans run on raw bytes / utf-8 decode. Add normalize(data)->text: BOM sniff, NUL-interleave heuristic, utf-16 decode, gunzip, then scan both raw and normalized. .reg files and PS 'Unicode' saves are UTF-16LE by default.\"},\n154\t  {\"id\": \"descriptor-syntax-generic\", \"concept\": \"descriptor literal in non-`=` languages and multi-line materials\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n155\t   \"detail\": \"analyse_v3 regex is `descriptor_\\\\w*\\\\s*=` (case-sensitive): misses Tcl `set descriptor_x {..}`, R `<-`, Go/Make `:=`, Rust `const X: &str =`, Ruby `DESCRIPTOR_X =`, YAML `descriptor_x: |`, XML elements (D14 relied on the comment marker alone). Also the marker material can wrap across lines (YAML block scalar, =begin, <# #>, triple quotes): join continuation lines before peeling.\"},\n156\t  {\"id\": \"container-carrier-extract\", \"concept\": \"script inside OLE/OOXML/XLM/OneNote/CHM/LNK/pyc/a3x/luac\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n157\t   \"detail\": \"Pure-python (gate forbids subprocess) member walker: zipfile for OOXML + vbaProject.bin via olefile, LNK string data (LnkParse3), CHM via 7z-style ITSF directory, OneNote FileDataStoreObject GUID scan, gzip; emit every text stream to the plan scanner. Oracles for fixtures: olevba, .venv/bin/xtone, xtchm, lnk, xtpyi (all installed).\"},\n158\t  {\"id\": \"prebuild-lane-config-script\", \"concept\": \"hctf prebuild has no script-analysis lane\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\",\n159\t   \"detail\": \"hctf/prebuild.py LANES lists metadata-forensics, warmups, binary only. Add a script-analysis entry (writable lib/scripts_prebuilt/ + tests/data/script_fixtures/, gate = codec tests + regress_lane script-analysis) so the 4 prebuild targets above can race at drop time.\"},\n160\t  {\"id\": \"ps-layer-peel\", \"concept\": \"PowerShell -EncodedCommand / FromBase64String+Deflate/Gzip / -f / -join [char] / env-substring\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n161\t   \"detail\": \"Static peeler for the Invoke-Obfuscation family: UTF-16LE b64, DeflateStream/GzipStream b64, format-operator reorder, [char] joins, `+` concat, backtick strip, $env:comspec/$PSHome index table. Oracle: .venv/bin/ps1 (refinery AST deob) + pwsh decode-only expressions. High value only if a polyglot-powershell / psm1 day comes.\"},\n162\t  {\"id\": \"batch-substring-emulation\", \"concept\": \"DOSfuscation %VAR:~n,m%, %VAR:a=b%, ^ carets, cmd /V:ON\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n163\t   \"detail\": \"solver batch emulator handles %/!/call/for joins only. Add substring/substitution/caret handling; oracle .venv/bin/bat (refinery emulator). Batch is the lane's synthetic-label language, so a 'batch advanced' fixture set is plausible.\"},\n164\t  {\"id\": \"xslt-msxsl-route\", \"concept\": \"XSLT with msxsl:script (wmic /format, msxsl.exe)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n165\t   \"detail\": \"lxml: collect <msxsl:script> and <ms:script> CDATA, route by language= attr to the JS/VBS paths; marker likely in <!-- -->. Same shape as D9 SCT and D14 MSBuild hosts.\"},\n166\t  {\"id\": \"gzip-zlib-codec-rep\", \"concept\": \"compressed reps in Codec_ consts\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n167\t   \"detail\": \"lib.codec REPS/TRANSFORMS lack gzip/zlib/deflate/base32/base85/rot13/atbash/rc4. Add as generic readings in _fallback (shape: H4sI, eJ, [A-Z2-7]=) and transform candidates (rot13, rc4 with stated key).\"},\n168\t  {\"id\": \"php-eval-chain\", \"concept\": \"eval(gzinflate(base64_decode(str_rot13(..)))) chains\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\",\n169\t   \"detail\": \"Parse the nested call chain and apply each named function innermost-first (base64_decode, gzinflate=raw deflate, gzuncompress=zlib, gzdecode=gzip, str_rot13, strrev, hex2bin, urldecode, convert_uudecode). Same pattern for Ruby/Python/Perl decode chains (unpack('m'), pack('H*'), zlib.decompress).\"},\n170\t  {\"id\": \"python-exec-layers\", \"concept\": \"marshal/zlib/base64 exec onion (pyobfuscate, BlankOBF)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\",\n171\t   \"detail\": \"Worker recipe, not a module: replace exec/eval with a capture and run under python3 -I in an empty dir; marshal blobs -> pycdc/xdis with matching magic. lib.pyc.recover_python already covers real pyinstaller/pyc carriers.\"},\n172\t  {\"id\": \"php-cli\", \"concept\": \"PHP CLI for lint/tokenize\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\",\n173\t   \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y php-cli  (php -l, token_get_all; never run fixtures). PHP is a carried language since D8.\"},\n174\t  {\"id\": \"lua-unluac\", \"concept\": \"Lua interpreter + bytecode decompiler\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\",\n175\t   \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y lua5.4 luajit ; unluac.jar from https://sourceforge.net/projects/unluac/ into tools/unluac (java 25 installed) with bin/unluac wrapper. Needed if a luac-compiled carrier variant of the D9 Lua fixtures appears.\"},\n176\t  {\"id\": \"xsltproc-cabextract-yq\", \"concept\": \"XML/CAB/YAML helpers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\",\n177\t   \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y xsltproc cabextract ; yq: pip install yq into .venv (jq wrapper; jq installed). xsltproc only for --noout lint, never to apply a stylesheet.\"},\n178\t  {\"id\": \"tcl-r-interpreters\", \"concept\": \"tclsh / Rscript for syntax checks\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\",\n179\t   \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y tcl (small); r-base-core is ~100 MB, install only on an R day. Static reading is enough for v=3 plans.\"},\n180\t  {\"id\": \"applescript-scpt\", \"concept\": \"compiled AppleScript (.scpt FasdUAS) disassembly\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\",\n181\t   \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Jinmo/applescript-disassembler into tools/ (pure python). D13 shipped source .applescript only; a compiled variant would hide the marker in UTF-16/MacRoman strings.\"},\n182\t  {\"id\": \"js-deob-extras\", \"concept\": \"synchrony / JSFuck decoding\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\",\n183\t   \"detail\": \"npm i deobfuscator (synchrony CLI) into tools/npm; webcrack (installed) already handles obfuscator.io; JSFuck/JJencode via js_sandbox capture of the final call.\"},\n184\t  {\"id\": \"ps-deob-modules\", \"concept\": \"PowerDecode / PSDecode for pwsh\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\",\n185\t   \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Malandrone/PowerDecode and https://github.com/R3MRUM/PSDecode into tools/ (pwsh 7.6.6 installed). refinery ps1 covers most; these add layer-by-layer IEX override tracing.\"},\n186\t  {\"id\": \"xlm-standalone\", \"concept\": \"XLMMacroDeobfuscator CLI\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\",\n187\t   \"detail\": \"uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python XLMMacroDeobfuscator  (refinery xlmdeobf is an inlined port and already works; standalone gives --sort-formulas/--extract-only).\"},\n188\t  {\"id\": \"dotnet-script\", \"concept\": \"csx inspection\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\",\n189\t   \"detail\": \"dotnet tool install --tool-path tools/dotnet-tools dotnet-script  (only to parse; ilspycmd covers compiled InstallUtil/MSBuild payloads).\"},\n190\t  {\"id\": \"leaf-ext-list\", \"concept\": \"nested-zip sniff skips unknown leaf extensions\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\",\n191\t   \"detail\": \"_LEAF_EXT in solve.py still lacks .lua .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl (and future .rb .tcl .r .groovy .kts .go .rs .awk .yml .tf .xsl .reg .inf). Speed only (~1 s); prefer sniffing PK magic over an extension list.\"},\n192\t  {\"id\": \"new-synthetic-label-family\", \"concept\": \"code-shape labels for a new language (D2-D7 style)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\",\n193\t   \"detail\": \"Polyglot days have been plan-verbatim since D8, but an 'advanced <lang>' set (like bash-advanced) would bring feature/primitive or control/style labels. Apply playbook NAMING LAWS; probe one field per submit; check run_for_time regime first.\"},\n194\t  {\"id\": \"family-name-underscore\", \"concept\": \"host-type families like polyglot-github_actions / host-<profile>-<lang>\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\",\n195\t   \"detail\": \"Keep the longest-known-suffix field parse; derive the family prefix from the contract ids, never from the file stem (D14 msbuild_xml).\"}\n196\t]\n197\t```\n198\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4153782f-037b-4711-a30f-5c4f9282a477","uuid":"554e1299-836a-49db-970d-c5b18e338a32","timestamp":"2026-10-16T13:16:34.451Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/4153782f-037b-4711-a30f-5c4f9282a477/tool-results/b1vpv7a54.txt","content":"# script-analysis — coverage atlas (D1-D15 seen vs. D16+ candidates)\n\nBuilt 2026-10-15 after D15 (1026 ids, 116 members). Read with `reference/techniques/script-analysis.md` (what the GM\nactually asked) — this file is the BREADTH map: which common script/malware-script CTF concepts we have met, which we\nhave not, how to fingerprint and statically decode each, and what to prebuild/install before they drop.\n\nContext that drives the likelihood column:\n- Since D8 every new language is a **v=3 polyglot**: 4 fixtures `polyglot-<lang>-{benign-utility,downloader,launcher,\n  staged-chain}` (44 ids: role/attack/adapter/campaign/steps/stage-count/host-profile/obfuscation/stage-profile/\n  next-language + url) plus sometimes one `host-<profile>-<lang>` file. All answers are plan-verbatim; the plan sits\n  behind `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG>-..` in the host's comment syntax + a `descriptor_<id>` literal.\n  The D15 solver (`challenges/day15/scripting-crumb-trail/solver/solve.py`, `V3_MARK` / `_v3_peel` / `analyse_v3`)\n  is language-agnostic **as long as** the marker is ASCII/UTF-8 in raw bytes, on one line, peelable by hex/base64/\n  reverse within 3 layers. The real D16+ risk is not a new language — it is a new **carrier/encoding/container** or a\n  new **synthetic-label family** (the D2-D7 style/control/expansion era).\n- Family names may contain `_` (D14 `polyglot-msbuild_xml`); host profiles seen: standalone, wsf_jscript, wsf_mixed,\n  hta_jscript, php_webshell, sct_scriptlet, lua_openresty, perl_cgi. D14 picked a Windows LOLBin (MSBuild), D10 a WMI\n  host (MOF), D13 a macOS host: the organizers alternate \"language\" days and \"trusted-host abuse\" days.\n- ~16 drops left (D16-D31). Paths below: `$R=/home/testpwn/huntress-2026`; `source bin/env.sh` puts `bin/` on PATH\n  (pwsh 7.6.6, box-js, js-beautify, webcrack, pycdc/pycdas, 7z, autoit-ripper, ilspycmd). `R/.venv/bin` holds oletools,\n  msoffcrypto-tool, decompyle3/uncompyle6/xdis, pyinstxtractor-ng, LnkParse3, chepy, lxml, and **binary refinery 0.11.1**\n  (AST deobfuscators `ps1` `js` `vba`, batch emulator `bat`, `wshenc`, `xlmdeobf`, `xtone`, `xtchm`, `lnk`, `xtpyi`,\n  `pyc`, `a3x`, `xtnode`, `decompress`, `b64`, `xor`, `rot`...). Usage: `.venv/bin/<unit> < file`.\n\n## 1. Concept table\n\nLegend: INSTALLED = verified with `which`/`.venv/bin` on 2026-10-15; MISSING = not on the box. Never execute a\nfixture's behaviour: run only decoders / AST deobfuscators / emulators on extracted literals.\n\n| # | concept | status | recognition cues | standard tool / approach + exact command | D16+ likelihood |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | PowerShell `.ps1` (v=1 JSON descriptor, `$nativeTypes`) | seen D1 | `$encodedMaterial=[Convert]::FromBase64String(..)`, `function artifact_<hex>`, `[pscustomobject]@{..}` | `base64 -d`; `.venv/bin/ps1 < f.ps1` (INSTALLED, AST deob); `pwsh -NoProfile -NonInteractive -c '<decode expr only>'` (INSTALLED) | carried daily |\n| 2 | JScript WSH `.js` | seen D2 | `ActiveXObject`, `WScript.`, `decode_*/recover_*/inspect_*`, `\"52:90:..\"` | `node $R/hctf/js_sandbox.js f.js`; `box-js --no-kill f.js` (INSTALLED); `.venv/bin/js < f.js` | carried daily |\n| 3 | Batch `.bat/.cmd` + expansion (%/!/call/for) | seen D3 | `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:`, `setlocal EnableDelayedExpansion`, `call set %%..%%` | Python cmd-expansion emulation (solver `batchplan.py`); `.venv/bin/bat < f.bat` (INSTALLED, refinery emulator prints command lines) | carried daily |\n| 4 | VBScript `.vbs` | seen D4 | `Const Codec_<id>`, `Chr(`, `On Error Resume Next`, `Select Case` | lib.codec from the Codec const; `.venv/bin/vba < f.vbs` (INSTALLED) | carried daily |\n| 5 | Python carriers (pyinstaller/pyarmor/py2exe/cx_Freeze/zipapp/wheel/pyc38) | seen D5 (recovered `.py`), D6 TT real cx_Freeze binary | `*-recovered.py`, `MATERIAL_<id>`, `CODEC_<id>`; binary: `MEI\\x0c\\x0b\\x0a\\x0b\\x0e`, `PYZ`, `library.zip` | `lib.pyc.recover_python(path)`; `pyinstxtractor-ng x.exe`; `pycdc f.pyc` / `decompyle3 f.pyc` (all INSTALLED); `.venv/bin/xtpyi -l < x.exe` | med: a real frozen binary variant |\n| 6 | Bash `.sh` + bash-advanced (`Feature_<id>`) | seen D6/D7-D14 | `readonly Material_`, `${!ptr}`, `local -A`, `trap`, here-strings | lib.codec; never run bash; `bash -n f.sh` (syntax only) | carried; +2 fixtures some days |\n| 7 | Node ESM `.mjs` | seen D7 | `import`, top-level `await`, `process.env.HUNTRESS_INSPECT_ONLY`, `Buffer.from` | lib.codec static; `webcrack f.mjs -o out/` (INSTALLED) | carried daily |\n| 8 | PHP polyglot + webshell host | seen D8 | `<?php`, `$descriptor_<id>`, `eval(`/`assert(`, `$_POST`/`$_REQUEST` | V3_MARK peel; `php` MISSING (`apt install php-cli` for `php -l`/token dump only) | carried daily |\n| 9 | WSF / HTA hosts | seen D8 | `<job><script language=..>`, `<hta:application>`, mixed JScript+VBS | extract each `<script>` body (lxml/bs4 INSTALLED) and route by language | carried |\n| 10 | Lua + OpenResty host | seen D9 | `local descriptor_`, `--` comments, `ngx.`, `inert_handler_<id>` | V3_MARK; `lua`/`luac` MISSING (`apt install lua5.4`) | carried |\n| 11 | SCT scriptlet (regsvr32 /i:url scrobj.dll, Squiblydoo) | seen D9 (host) | `<?xml?><scriptlet><registration progid=..>`, `<![CDATA[` | strip CDATA -> JScript/VBS route | carried |\n| 12 | WMI MOF | seen D10 | `#pragma namespace`, `instance of __EventFilter`, `ActiveScriptEventConsumer`, `ScriptText =` | V3_MARK; ScriptText is a C-escaped JS/VBS string -> unescape then route | carried |\n| 13 | TypeScript | seen D11 | type annotations, `interface`, `as const`, `.ts` | V3_MARK; no tsc needed (strip types or read literals) | carried |\n| 14 | AutoIt `.au3` | seen D12 | `Global Const $descriptor_`, `;` comments, `#include <..>`, `Execute(`, `BinaryToString` | V3_MARK; compiled: `autoit-ripper x.exe out/` / `.venv/bin/a3x < x.a3x` (INSTALLED) | carried; compiled a3x = med |\n| 15 | AppleScript (source) | seen D13 | `property descriptor_<id> :`, `--` comments, `do shell script`, `osascript -e` | V3_MARK; compiled `.scpt` (`FasdUAS` magic) = no decompiler (MISSING: applescript-disassembler) | carried; `.scpt` = low/med |\n| 16 | MSBuild `.proj` inline task | seen D14 | `<Project xmlns=..msbuild..>`, `<UsingTask TaskFactory=\"CodeTaskFactory\">`, `<Code Type=\"Fragment\">` C# CDATA, `<HuntressDescriptor>` | V3_MARK in `<!-- -->`; lxml for the property element | carried |\n| 17 | Perl `.pl` + perl_cgi host | seen D15 | `#!/usr/bin/env perl`, `use strict;`, `my $descriptor_`, `print \"Content-Type:` | V3_MARK; `perl -MO=Deparse f.pl` (INSTALLED, parse-only, BEGIN blocks still run - strip them) | carried |\n| 18 | Ruby `.rb` (+ ERB/Rack/Rails host) | gap | `require`, `def ..end`, `puts`, `#{}` interpolation, `=begin/=end`, `.unpack1('m0')`, `Base64.decode64`, `eval`/`instance_eval`, `<%= %>` | `ruby -c f.rb` (INSTALLED /usr/bin/ruby, syntax only); `ruby -e 'print ARGV[0].unpack1(\"m\")' <b64>`; Ruby CONSTANTS are uppercase -> descriptor may be `DESCRIPTOR_X =` | **high**: last major mainstream script language; ruby already installed |\n| 19 | PowerShell module / `.psm1` `.psd1` `.ps1xml` (v=3 polyglot-powershell) | gap (PS only v=1) | `Export-ModuleMember`, `FunctionsToExport`, `<Types><Type><ScriptMethod><Script>`, `<#  #>` block comments (marker may sit inside `<# #>`) | `.venv/bin/ps1 < f.psm1`; lxml for ps1xml `<Script>` nodes | **high**: PS is the canonical malware language and has no v=3 fixture |\n| 20 | Tcl / Expect | gap | `#!/usr/bin/tclsh`, `set descriptor_x \"...\"` (no `=`!), `proc`, `puts`, `binary decode base64`, `{braces}` strings | `tclsh` MISSING (`apt install tcl`); static: regex `set\\s+descriptor_\\w+\\s+[\"{]` | med |\n| 21 | R script | gap | `<-` assignment, `library(`, `base64enc::`, `rawToChar(`, `system(`, `#` comments | `Rscript` MISSING (`apt install r-base-core`, big); static `<-` descriptor regex | low/med |\n| 22 | Groovy / Jenkinsfile | gap | `pipeline { agent .. stages`, `sh '''..'''`, `def x = \"..\"`, `\"cmd\".execute()`, `.decodeBase64()` | `groovy` MISSING (java INSTALLED; jar from apache); static read | med: CI-abuse host fits \"trusted toolchain\" theme |\n| 23 | Kotlin script `.kts` / Gradle `build.gradle.kts` | gap | `val descriptor_x = \"..\"`, `plugins {`, `tasks.register`, `Runtime.getRuntime().exec`, `Base64.getDecoder()` | `kotlinc` MISSING; static | med (Gradle build abuse) |\n| 24 | Go (`go run`, `//go:generate`) | gap | `package main`, `descriptor_x := \"..\"` (`:=` breaks current regex), `exec.Command`, raw `` `..` `` strings | `go vet f.go` (INSTALLED /usr/bin/go; never `go run`) | med |\n| 25 | Rust script / `build.rs` | gap | `fn main()`, `const DESCRIPTOR_X: &str = \"..\"`, `std::process::Command`, `r#\"..\"#` raw strings, `\\u{..}` | `rustc` INSTALLED (don't build); static | low/med (`build.rs` = build-time abuse) |\n| 26 | AWK program | gap | `BEGIN {`, `system(`, `\"cmd\" \\| getline`, `#!/usr/bin/awk -f` | `gawk --lint -f f.awk /dev/null` is NOT safe (BEGIN runs) -> static only | med (LOLBin `awk`, GTFOBins) |\n| 27 | sed script | gap | `#!/bin/sed -f`, `s/../../e` (GNU exec flag), `w /path` | static | low |\n| 28 | Makefile | gap | `target: deps` + TAB recipes, `$(shell ..)`, `DESCRIPTOR := ..` (`:=`), `.PHONY` | `make -n -f Makefile` (INSTALLED; dry run still evaluates `$(shell)` -> static only) | med (build-system abuse theme) |\n| 29 | Dockerfile | gap | `FROM`, `RUN curl .. \\| sh`, `ENV`, `ARG`, `# HUNTRESS..` comments, `COPY --chmod` | static; `docker` INSTALLED (never build) | med |\n| 30 | CI YAML (GitHub Actions / GitLab CI) | gap | `on: [push]`, `jobs:`, `runs-on:`, `steps: - run:` + block scalar, `stages:`, `script:`; block scalars span lines | `.venv/bin/python -c 'import yaml,sys;print(yaml.safe_load(open(sys.argv[1])))' f.yml` (INSTALLED); `yq` MISSING | med/high: supply-chain host, family would be `polyglot-github_actions`-style |\n| 31 | Ansible playbook | gap | `- hosts:`, `tasks:`, `ansible.builtin.shell:`, `become: true`, `vars:` | yaml.safe_load (INSTALLED); ansible MISSING (not needed) | low/med |\n| 32 | Terraform HCL | gap | `resource \"null_resource\"`, `pr