\"Classify the decoded ordered behavior graph by its complete terminal intent. Use benign_utility for decode_configuration then return_configuration; stager for acquire_remote then memory/pipe dispatch; dropper for decode_embedded then write_file; downloader for acquire_remote then write_file; uploader for a graph ending in upload_remote or transmit_remote; launcher for locate_local then dispatch_process; impact for a transform ending in write_recovery_note; staged_chain for a multi-stage profile/acquire followed by write and terminal dispatch_process (with optional decode_embedded or change_mode steps) or for a graph ending in handoff_script; relay for decode_configuration then locate_interpreter then dispatch_next_stage; and persistence_descriptor for build_schedule then register_descriptor. Earlier preparation steps do not override the terminal graph.\",\n      \"artifact\": \"evidence.zip -> host-context.js\",\n      \"answer_format\": {\n        \"kind\": \"enum\",\n        \"accepted_values\": [\n          \"benign_utility\",\n          \"stager\",\n          \"dropper\",\n          \"downloader\",\n          \"uploader\",\n          \"launcher\",\n          \"impact\",\n          \"staged_chain\",\n          \"relay\",\n          \"persistence_descriptor\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"normalization\": \"trim\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"jscript-benign-attack\",\n      \"question\": \"Map the decoded ordered behavior graph to one primary MITRE ATT&CK technique using this precedence: a terminal handoff_script or dispatch_next_stage makes the staged chain or relay the specimen's language-specific Command and Scripting Interpreter sub-technique even when acquire_remote or decode_configuration appears earlier; otherwise decode_configuration followed by return_configuration is benign/none, acquire_remote is ingress transfer, decode_embedded is deobfuscation/decoding, upload_remote or transmit_remote is exfiltration over the command-and-control channel, dispat