{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg5yqJ7MfVr62UKV51N4a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Hvt5Ae8vnXrnhq5RNs5fXd","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/script-analysis.md","content":"# script-analysis — technique log (days 1-16; updated after every day)\n\nHow this lane has looked so far (these are observations, not guarantees):\n- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field.\n- One AES zip `evidence.zip` (password `infected`) of inert \"Huntress Script Triage\" fixtures. **The contract is CUMULATIVE**:\n  each day keeps every earlier file/question and adds one language; bytes and values re-roll daily. PS (d1, 15 ids) ->\n  +JScript (d2, 87) -> +Batch (d3, 159) -> +VBScript (d4, 231) -> +Python (d5, 357) -> +Bash (d6, 399) -> +Node `.mjs` + Bash\n  advanced (d7, 469) -> +PHP polyglot + WSF/HTA/PHP-webshell hosts (d8, 615) -> +Lua + SCT/OpenResty hosts (d9, 695) -> +WMI MOF\n  (d10, 753) -> +TypeScript (d11, 811) -> +AutoIt (d12, 855) -> +AppleScript (d13, 913) -> +MSBuild `.proj` (d14, 971) -> +Perl\n  + perl_cgi host (d15, 1026) -> +Ruby `.rb` + ruby_rack host (d16, 1095; 123 members). Most days also add 2 Bash advanced\n  fixtures (not d12, d15). Since D8 the TITLE/PROMPT is a pun or narrative; the new language shows up only in the member list\n  (D16 \"Same Same, But Different\" = \"obfuscation equivalence\", and the new files were Ruby). Diff the contract ids against yesterday's.\n- From day 2 on, every fixture hides a **self-describing plan**: `v=N|steps=a,b|adapter=..|stage_count=..|campaign_id=..|<indicators>`.\n  It sits behind a codec, usually named in a `Codec_<id>` / `CODEC_<id>` / `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` const of the form `rep|transform|key`.\n  Most exact_text answers are plan values copied verbatim. From D8 there is also a **`v=3` plan**: it carries `role=` and `attack=`\n  itself, and sits behind a `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-` comment.\n- The hard part is **naming CODE SHAPE**: control-flow, expansion, and function/invocation/property styles. These are GM synthetic\n  labels that are not in the plan. Role and scenario are enums, so read `accepted_values`.\n- Files are named by behaviour (host-context, memory-stage, embedded-write, remote-write, local-dispatch, staged-handoff/-chain,\n  outbound-transfer, impact-plan, relay-handoff, schedule-descriptor). Answer-id = `<lang>-<role>-<field>`; the artifact path picks\n  the file. Don't trust the file name over the plan `steps`.\n- Narrative prompts (D8 \"doesn't match its siblings\", D15 \"a store that was never there\", D16 \"prove which ones are truly\n  equivalent, expose the variant that quietly changed the plot\") have NEVER been asked as a question. Answer the contract ids only.\n- Time Trial windows ~5-17 s. Mastery has `setN.` ids: 2 sets d2-d7 and d10-d14, **5 sets d8, d9, d15 (5130 ids) and d16 (5475\n  ids)**. The artifact was `evidence-0N.zip`, `delivery N: evidence.zip` (d6), or one `evidence-01.zip` holding every\n  `evidence-0N.zip` (d7-d9). Same-named deliveries: pair by sha256. Timed questions carry `[assigned-artifact-sha256:<hex>]`.\n  From D15 the timed contracts are the untimed regular pool (`run_for_time:false`, `variant_fresh:true`, no deadline).\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants of the SAME day -- parse every value listed)\nEach miss cost one failed timed attempt + a ~45-90 s generalize cycle (D6: 4 cycles; D7: 1; D8-D14: 0; D15: TT localize + 1\nMastery cycle; D16: 0 answer misses -- the Mastery failures were runner timeouts, no bytes reached a verdict).\n- **GM label regime (batch `expansion`; D15 pool-keyed, D16 DATE-keyed)** -- SAME bytes, SAME question text, DIFFERENT label.\n  Old regime (every D3-D14 case + the D15 single): the whole handoff is labelled, `echo(!var!)` => `delayed` unless a FOR/h-pool\n  rule fires. Statement regime (D15 TT/Mastery `run_for_time:false`; **D16 single with NO run_for_time key**; D16 TT a719c002):\n  label the JOIN STATEMENT alone -- `!a!!b!` join = delayed; `for %%G in (..) do call set` = for_indirect for ANY pool (incl. an h\n  pool); bare `call set \"x=%%h0%%..\"` (h pool) = call_double; bare `call set` over item/v_a/FrAg pools = percent; plain\n  `set \"x=%a%%b%\"` = percent. D16 single GM labels: benign for_indirect, stager/dropper delayed, downloader call_double,\n  uploader/launcher/impact/chain/relay percent. The D15 rule \"branch on run_for_time\" was keyed on the wrong thing and cost 5\n  rejected probes on the D16 single. Parse rule: **statement regime is the default** (`run_for_time is False` OR\n  `started_at >= 2026-10-16`); the old regime only for older replayed cases. When byte-identical constructs get different GM\n  labels across cases, tabulate (construct, label) against EVERY contract key (started_at, run_for_time, variant_fresh,\n  hall_of_fame_eligible) at once instead of diffing bytes. Expect other synthetic labels (control/style) to flip the same way.\n- **Codec per file** -- rep x transform x key re-rolls per variant; never bind a role to the sample's codec. **NEW rep NAMES\n  appear only on variants** (D7 TT: `unicode_escapes`, `json_numbers`, `reversed_base64`, Bash `xor_hex|cd`). Decode by the\n  material's SHAPE (escapes / int array / hex / base64, each also reversed) x the named transform; accept only output starting\n  `v=`; the name only orders the tries. D9-D16: nothing beyond lib.codec's vocabulary (0 decode failures).\n- **Codec spec arity** -- `rep|transform|key`, `rep|` (empty transform = identity; Bash advanced D7-D16), or transform folded\n  into the rep with the key second (`xor_hex|cd`, D16 `xor_hex|ec`). Split on `|`, never index blindly (lib.codec `_spec`).\n- **Plan carrier tag (v=3, D8-D16)** -- `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-<data>` + the same data in a descriptor literal. Tags `B64`,\n  `HEX`, `HB64` (hex of base64), `FRAG` (hex split by `.` every 24 chars); stayed fixed per file in every delivery D8-D16, only\n  values re-rolled. Parse rule: ignore the tag name; peel by shape, recurse (max 3-4 layers); accept only `v=`. Tag =\n  `obfuscation_profile` (B64 base64, HEX plain_hex, HB64 hex_base64, FRAG fragmented_hex). `lib.codec.find_codecs(src)` returns it.\n- **Plan carrier host syntax (v=3)** -- marker in whatever comment the host uses: `//` (PHP, JS, HTA, WSF, SCT, MOF, TS), `--`\n  (Lua, AppleScript), `;` (AutoIt), `<!-- -->` (MSBuild), `#` (Perl D15, Ruby D16). Descriptor forms: `$descriptor_<id>`,\n  `var/local descriptor_<id>`, `Global Const $descriptor_<id>`, `property descriptor_<id> :`, `<HuntressDescriptor>` element\n  (MSBuild, no name), `my $descriptor_<id> = \"..\";` (Perl), **`DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX> = \"..\"` uppercase Ruby constant (D16)**. Parse rule:\n  regex `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V\\d+\\s*:\\s*(\\w*)-?\\s*([^\\s\"'<>\\]]+)` over raw bytes, independent of comment syntax, case and extension.\n- **Numeric literal radix** -- decimal `23,7`, hex `0x17`, or a joined string read with `parseInt(x, R)` / `int(x, R)`: READ THE\n  RADIX FROM THE CODE (D6 JScript TT hex; Mastery dash-joined DECIMALS). Applies to keys too.\n- **Base64 alphabet** -- standard and urlsafe (`-` `_`) both occur; whitelist and pad (D6 Python TT).\n- **Reversal level** -- `reversed_hex/_decimal/_integer_list` reverse the LIST; `reversed_base64` reverses the TEXT. Try both.\n- **Carrier of the same language** -- plain source vs a frozen executable (D6 TT: Python plan in a cx_Freeze build). Locate\n  material by markers (`MATERIAL_`/`CODEC_`/`v=`/`HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_`), not by file type.\n- **Material layout** -- one literal, split chunks, `+=`, adjacent quoted strings, `.`-separated FRAG; join before decoding.\n- **Adapter values** re-roll within a role (Node stager http_then_module/https_then_vm/fetch_then_function; launcher\n  execfile_node/fork_module/spawn_file; persistence systemd_descriptor/npm_lifecycle_descriptor) -- always plan-verbatim.\n- **Transport/runner, not variant** -- D7 TT saved `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` as the zip; D8 TT start 503\n  `training_rotation_invalid`; D16 Mastery (5 sets, 5475 ids, 3.2-3.7 MB status bodies at 5-8 s each) hit the 60 s local\n  `hb_timed` cap on all 5 attempts (`exec_error`, nothing submitted). None of these is a solver change; never harvest them as cases.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n| You see | First move |\n|---|---|\n| `evidence.zip`, \"method=AES Encrypted\" | Triage already extracted it (`work/extracted/`) and decoded every plan. Diff the member list / contract ids against yesterday's to find the new language (D16: 4 `polyglot-ruby-*.rb` + `host-ruby-rack-ruby.rb` + 2 `.sh`). Triage used to skip new extensions (D7 `.mjs`, D8 `.php`, D9 `.lua`); D15-D16 it decoded them. Open members with `lib.common.read_member` (zipfile can't read AES). |\n| Prior-day languages in the contract | Cumulative: rerun the carried marker-routed solver FIRST (D9-D16: it covered each new v=3 language unchanged). Spend thinking on the new language and on synthetic-label regimes. |\n| `.ps1` `$encodedMaterial = [Convert]::FromBase64String('..')` + `$nativeTypes` | `base64 -d` -> JSON descriptor: url/wallet/mutex/UA/file/ext/note by SHAPE. `$nativeTypes` gives the scenario: Process/Registry+wallet=resource, ZipFile/HttpWebRequest=collection, Aes/DirectoryInfo=impact. |\n| `.js` WSH, `decode_*`/`recover_*`/`inspect_*`, XOR key arrays, `\"52:90:..\"` | Run each file in an empty `node` `vm` (no require/ActiveXObject, `eval` -> capture); keep the first object with `steps`. Styles come off the `inspect_*` body. |\n| `.bat/.cmd` `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` / `HUNTRESS-MATERIAL:`, `set \"itemN=..`, `:HUNTRESS_INSPECT` | Plan is in `set` fragments. Emulate cmd expansion in Python. MATERIAL = second encoded copy to cross-check. Expansion label: statement regime by default (Variant axes). Never run cmd. |\n| `.vbs` `Const Material_<id>`, `Const Codec_<id> = \"rep|transform|key\"` | Decode from the Codec const; rep/transform answers = Codec fields 1/2 verbatim. Control = construct wrapping `Decode_` inside `Recover_`. |\n| `.py` `*-recovered.py` with `MATERIAL_<id>`, `CODEC_<id>` | Decode from CODEC (or AST-whitelisted `decode_(load_(..))`). Plan v=2 carries syntax/obfuscation/carrier/windows_chain verbatim. |\n| `.sh` `readonly Material_<id>` + `readonly Codec_<id>` (+ `Feature_<id>()`) | Decode from the Codec const (multi-byte key = COMMA list). `Feature_` fixtures: role `advanced_syntax`, feature/primitive/campaign/stage_count/steps plan-verbatim, attack T1059.004. Never run bash. |\n| `.mjs` ESM `const Material_<id>`, async `load_/decode_/recover_/inspect_/plan_<id>` | Static decode (`lib.codec.find_codecs` + shape fallback). Don't run it. Plan fields verbatim; role from `steps`. |\n| `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG>-..` in any comment + a descriptor literal (`.php .lua .js(HTA/WSF/SCT) .vbs(WSF) .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb`) | **Route by the marker before the extension.** Peel to `v=3|language=..|role=..|attack=..|adapter=..|host_profile=..|obfuscation_profile=..|stage_profile=..|next_language=..|stage_count=..|steps=..|campaign_id=..|url=..|file_path=..`. EVERY answer incl. role/attack is plan-verbatim. |\n| Timed contract `run_for_time:false`, or any contract started on/after 2026-10-16 | Batch `expansion` = statement-only table. Check the contract keys before trusting labels harvested from older cases. |\n| Real `.pyc` / PyInstaller / pyarmor (not seen yet) | `lib.pyc.recover_python(path)` (pyinstxtractor-ng + decompyle3, `dis` fallback). |\n| `Codec_` key like `ba` / `0a` / `ec` | A hex byte. Transforms are ENCODE-side names: `subtract_modulo_256` decodes by ADDING; `rolling_xor` = c ^ previous CIPHER byte, seeded with the key. |\n\n## Codec table (`Codec_<id>='<rep>|<transform>|<key>'`, batch `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:<rep>|<transform>`; seen D3-D16)\n**Already done for you:** triage.md's \"Decoded payloads\" runs `lib.codec` on every declared codec (and a node vm sandbox on\nJScript). In solve.py: `lib.codec.find_codecs(text)` / `lib.codec.decode(material, rep, transform, key)` (pure Python,\nunknown names -> None). `NOT decoded by lib.codec` = new rep/transform/arity: decode by shape, note it under `## Proposed lib additions`.\n- Reps: base64_literal/_chunks, urlsafe_base64, reversed_base64; hex_pairs/_compact/_colon/_dash/_escape (`\\x`)/_literal (`0x`)/\n  _buffer/_array, percent_hex, escaped_octets, unicode_escapes; decimal_bytes/_comma/_dash/_pipe/_dot/_colon/_space/_csv/_array,\n  json_numbers, integer_list/_tuple, octal_space; reversed_text/_hex/_decimal/_integer_list; plain/split_fragments; v=3 hex_base64.\n- Transforms (key hex, multi-byte = COMMA list): identity (also EMPTY), reverse/reverse_bytes, single_byte_xor, repeating_key_xor,\n  reverse_then_xor, rolling_xor (2 flavours), add_modulo_256 (decode SUBTRACTS), subtract_modulo_256 (decode ADDS); batch names\n  carry the parameter: xor_5a, add_7 (decimal), rotate_left, reverse_xor; bash `xor_hex|<key>` = unhex then XOR.\n- Check: plaintext starts `v=` (or `{` JSON). If not, the codec reading is wrong.\n\n## Day by day\n**D1-D7 (PS -> +JScript -> +Batch -> +VBScript -> +Python -> +Bash -> +Node, 469 ids)**: D1 collection ATT&CK cost 5 wrong before\n`T1555.003`; D2 handoff = `staged_chain`, 7 wrong ATT&CK guesses; **D3 ~1 h 45 min, ~127 rejected probes** on batch\nexpansion/control labels -> NAMING LAWS; D4 VBS control probed one field at a time (4 wrong); D5-D6 0 wrong (~4 min; stage_count =\nplan field); D7 469/469 in ~100 s, TT missed 15 ids on new reps + one `rate_limited` body saved as the zip.\n**D8-D15 (+PHP polyglot & hosts, Lua/SCT/OpenResty, MOF, TS, AutoIt, AppleScript, MSBuild, Perl; 615 -> 1026 ids)**: D8 introduced\nv=3 (copy role/attack/adapter/profiles, don't derive); 6 ids lost once to hyphenated family names. Each new language = 4 polyglots\n(benign_utility/downloader/launcher/staged_chain; attack none/T1105/T1059/T1059; adapter local_parser/http_client/process_builder/\noperation_graph; campaign `<LANG>-<8hex>`, url `https://<lang>-<10hex>.example.invalid/stage`, file_path\n`/tmp/huntress-<lang>/.<16hex>.stage`) + sometimes one `host-<profile>-<lang>` file. D14 family had an underscore (`msbuild_xml`)\nand its prompt's ATT&CK (T1127.001) was NOT the answer (plan said T1059). D8-D14 all modes first try. D15: single 1026/1026 at\nT+17 s; TT and Mastery (5 sets) missed ~25 batch-expansion ids -> the label-regime axis; CORRECT ~5.5 min after start.\n**D16 Same Same, But Different (`obfuscation-equivalence`; +4 Ruby `.rb` polyglot + `host-ruby-rack-ruby.rb` + Bash advanced\n`ansi-c-quoting.sh`, `regex-conditional.sh`; 1095 ids, 123 members)**:\n- Prompt: \"several obfuscation families scrambled the same logic ... prove which are truly equivalent, expose the variant that\n  quietly changed the plot\". Flavour only: no equivalence/outlier question; every id was the usual per-file family.\n- Ruby fixture: `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..` + `DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX> = \"..\"` (uppercase constant). Plan v=3 `language=ruby`;\n  host_profile `standalone` / `ruby_rack` (host = staged_chain/T1059/operation_graph). `steps` answers are `>`-joined\n  (ordered_tokens), e.g. `profile_host>decode_configuration>dispatch_language`; stage_count is the plan field (benign = 2).\n  next_language values seen: powershell, jscript, batch, vbscript. All plan-verbatim; the carried solver decoded them unchanged.\n- Bash advanced (plan-verbatim): `ansi_c_quoting|ansi_c_escape_string` (`$'node\\nbash\\tfixture'`), `regex_conditional|\n  bash_regex_match` (`[[ $v =~ ^node-[0-9]+$ ]]`); codecs `hex_compact|` and `xor_hex|ec`.\n- Single: worker decided \"carried solver covers Ruby\" at T+33 s; the bisecting submit then hit 5 `incorrect` probes on\n  batch-{uploader,launcher,impact,chain,relay}-expansion (`delayed` -> GM `percent`): the single has NO run_for_time key yet used\n  the statement regime. Duel worker switched the regime on `started_at >= 2026-10-16`; CORRECT at T+4 min 23 s.\n- TT a719c002 (`run_for_time:false`): CORRECT first try, 16.7 s (start 6.3, download 2.1, solve 1.4, submit 6.9).\n- Mastery (5 sets, 5475 ids): 5/5 attempts `exec_error` \"local hb_timed timed out\" (60 s runner cap) -- the start/download/\n  submit of a 5475-id bundle does not fit the cap; no answers reached the GM, so no variant axis could be observed.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- **Check `answer_format.kind` first.** `enum` lists values (scenario, role). `mitre_attack_id` takes `T####[.###]` or literal\n  `none` (benign_utility). `integer`/`ordered_tokens` (d6+; steps joined with `>`). `exact_text` = plan value or synthetic label.\n- **Plan-verbatim fields** (copy exactly): adapter (COM ProgIDs `MSXML2.ServerXMLHTTP.6.0`, LOLBins `CertReq.exe`/`curl.exe`/\n  `cipher.exe`, batch `call`/`set`/`for`, Node `console_report`.., v=3 local_parser/runtime_loader/file_writer/http_client/\n  process_builder/schedule_builder/operation_graph); indicators (campaign_id, host_id, url, file_path, upload_url, next_stage,\n  extension, note_name, handoff_id, cron_path, schedule_path, service_name -- question reads \"exact X indicator\", X = plan key);\n  batch `graph` (linear/single/diamond/fan_out/fallback_retry/cross_language/same_language); Python syntax/obfuscation/carrier/\n  windows_chain; Bash feature/primitive (16 seen D7-D16); v=3 host_profile (standalone, wsf_jscript, wsf_mixed, hta_jscript,\n  php_webshell, sct_scriptlet, lua_openresty, perl_cgi, ruby_rack), obfuscation (base64/plain_hex/hex_base64/fragmented_hex),\n  stage_profile (single_descriptor/two_stage_download_execute/three_stage_decode_write_launch/cross_language_handoff), next_language.\n- **v=3 role and attack too.** GM accepted the plan's PARENT ids `T1059` (launcher, staged_chain, every host) and `T1053`\n  (persistence_descriptor). **v=3 role does NOT follow `steps`** (D14 MSBuild, D16 Ruby downloader steps\n  `acquire_remote>dispatch_process`) -- copy role= and steps= independently.\n- **Role from `steps`** (v=1/v=2 only): decode_configuration,return_configuration = benign_utility; acquire_remote +\n  dispatch_memory/pipe = stager; acquire_remote,write_file = downloader; decode_embedded,write_file = dropper; locate_local,\n  dispatch_process = launcher; read_file/upload,transmit_remote = uploader; transform + recovery_note = impact;\n  build_schedule,register_descriptor = persistence_descriptor; recognize_syntax,reconstruct_intent + `feature=` = advanced_syntax;\n  ends in handoff_script or profile_host..dispatch_process = staged_chain; dispatch_next_stage (Python) = relay.\n  cron_path/service_name on a staged_chain are indicators only, NOT persistence.\n- **Role -> ATT&CK** (v=1/v=2; `lib.scripts.role_attack(role, lang)`): benign `none`; downloader/stager T1105; dropper T1140;\n  uploader T1041; impact T1486; persistence_descriptor T1053.003; advanced_syntax T1059.004; launcher/staged_chain/relay = host\n  language T1059.003 batch / .004 bash / .005 VBS / .006 python / .007 JScript and Node. PS scenarios: resource_hijacking T1496,\n  synthetic_collection T1555.003, synthetic_impact T1486. REJECTED: T1218.010, T1620, T1027.009, T1005, T1560, T1119, T1074(.001);\n  stager T1059.007; dropper T1105.\n- **Batch expansion** (enum percent/delayed/call_double/for_indirect; question \"Classify only the expansion form used by the\n  descriptor reconstruction statement\"): statement regime = Variant axes table (default from D16). Old regime (D3-D14 cases):\n  h-pool + `call set` = call_double; `for .. do call set` over other pools = for_indirect; everything else delayed (incl.\n  `!h0!!h1!`). Fragment JOINER pitfall: `set \"item9=%item0%%item1%..\"` is the JOIN, not fragment 9. REJECTED: percent_expansion,\n  immediate, call-double, double_call.\n- **Batch control**: direct, errorlevel_guard (`ver >nul` + `if errorlevel 1 exit /b 1`), goto_dispatch, call_subroutine,\n  if_guard (`if defined X`); separators and `:HUNTRESS_UNUSED` dead labels are NOT control. ~45 synonyms rejected (D3).\n- **VBS control**: direct, select_case, do_once, while_once, error_guard (`On Error Resume Next`..`Err.Raise`), for_once.\n- **Codec labels**: representation/transform = the codec const's fields 1/2 VERBATIM (per-language spellings differ).\n- **JScript styles**: function-style `function f(` declaration / `var f = function(` anonymous_expression / `var f = function\n  f_body(` named_expression; invocation-style direct / call (`.call`, also via a local invoke helper) / apply; property-style\n  dot / bracket_literal / mixed (triage's `shape:` line counts them).\n- **NAMING LAWS** (proven on if_guard, error_guard, do_once, pe_cli): conditional/bail-out = `<keyword>_guard`; run-once loop =\n  `<keyword>_once`; control transfer = `<keyword>_<action>`. Spelled-out statements (if_defined, on_error_resume, do_exit,\n  while_wend) and descriptive synonyms (flag_guard, opaque_predicate) have ALWAYS been rejected.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **Regime keyed on the wrong contract field** (D16 single, 5 incorrect probes, ~1.5 min): yesterday's fix branched on\n  `run_for_time is False`; the GM moved the single solve to the statement regime too. When a carried label table breaks on\n  byte-identical constructs, assume the GM generator changed and re-check against EVERY contract key incl. `started_at`.\n- **Diffing bytes when the regime changed** (D15 Mastery, ~5 min): tabulate (construct, GM label) per contract key at once.\n- **Big Mastery bundles vs the local runner cap** (D16: 5475 ids, 5 x exec_error at 60 s). Status/contract bodies are 3-4 MB and\n  take 5-8 s each; a 5-set bundle needs start + download + solve + chunked submit (each <= 500 answers / 512 KiB). Report it to the\n  orchestrator as a budget problem; it is not a solver bug.\n- **Probing synonyms instead of deriving.** D3 lost ~1.5 h; apply the naming laws first; `hctf labels` seeds candidates.\n- **Per-set POST is all-or-nothing.** `--from-solver` bisects and prints the rejected id(s); probe uncertain label fields ONE\n  per submit (wrong cap is per field).\n- **Generic ATT&CK guesses** (d1, d2): use the role->ATT&CK table; a v=3 `attack=` is authoritative even as a parent id; a\n  prompt's ATT&CK hint (D14 T1127.001) is not.\n- **Routing by file extension** (D8-D9 `.js` held HTA/WSF/SCT, `.vbs` a WSF job): route by the plan marker first.\n- **Answer-id field parsing** (D8, 6 ids): family names contain hyphens/underscores; resolve the field as the longest known\n  `-<field>` suffix (`stage-count`/`stage-profile` before `stage`).\n- **GM error body saved as the artifact** (D7 TT): check size + sha256 against the start response first; tiny `{\"error\":..}` =\n  transport failure (re-download, exit non-zero), never a regression case.\n- **Stale notes travel with copied solvers** (D8-D16 `solver/NOTES.md` is still the D7 copy; D15-D16 regime fixes live only in\n  solve.py comments). Date every VARIANT AXIS line by day + attempt id; diagnose EVERY failed attempt.\n- **Unknown codec rep name -> silent no-plan** (D7 TT, 15 ids): fall back to material-shape readings.\n- **cmd parsing**: `%item0%` is a variable, not `%0`+`item`; CRLF/LF mixes and `SeT` casing occur. **Bash Codec key** comma\n  lists (`lib.scripts.codec_key()`). **stage_count != len(steps)**: read the plan field.\n- **Timed modes are a transport race** (D2 Mastery expired on downloads; D7 TT 13.5 s for 0.4 s of solving; D16 TT 16.7 s for\n  1.4 s). Fork per set and submit all sets in one call.\n- **Same-name deliveries**: pair Mastery files by sha256; if delivery 2 is missing, leave set 2 unanswered.\n- **Nested AES zips**: index the tree once; don't decrypt script leaves to sniff for PK (leaf-ext list still lacks `.lua .mof\n  .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb` -- speed only).\n- **Never execute fixtures.** Decode from the Codec const / descriptor plus a restricted interpreter; accept a plan only if it\n  parses as `k=v|..` with `steps` (or `feature`).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":686,"cache_read_input_tokens":93676,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":686},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4153782f-037b-4711-a30f-5c4f9282a477","uuid":"2ec3d2e4-2968-4e68-9c37-282f6bb65f20","timestamp":"2026-10-16T13:19:42.553Z","request_id":"req_011Cg5yqHknjoLKYru39tjEc","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Hvt5Ae8vnXrnhq5RNs5fXd":{"file_path":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/script-analysis.md","content":"# script-analysis — technique log (days 1-16; updated after every day)\n\nHow this lane has looked so far (these are observations, not guarantees):\n- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field.\n- One AES zip `evidence.zip` (password `infected`) of inert \"Huntress Script Triage\" fixtures. **The contract is CUMULATIVE**:\n  each day keeps every earlier file/question and adds one language; bytes and values re-roll daily. PS (d1, 15 ids) ->\n  +JScript (d2, 87) -> +Batch (d3, 159) -> +VBScript (d4, 231) -> +Python (d5, 357) -> +Bash (d6, 399) -> +Node `.mjs` + Bash\n  advanced (d7, 469) -> +PHP polyglot + WSF/HTA/PHP-webshell hosts (d8, 615) -> +Lua + SCT/OpenResty hosts (d9, 695) -> +WMI MOF\n  (d10, 753) -> +TypeScript (d11, 811) -> +AutoIt (d12, 855) -> +AppleScript (d13, 913) -> +MSBuild `.proj` (d14, 971) -> +Perl\n  + perl_cgi host (d15, 1026) -> +Ruby `.rb` + ruby_rack host (d16, 1095; 123 members). Most days also add 2 Bash advanced\n  fixtures (not d12, d15). Since D8 the TITLE/PROMPT is a pun or narrative; the new language shows up only in the member list\n  (D16 \"Same Same, But Different\" = \"obfuscation equivalence\", and the new files were Ruby). Diff the contract ids against yesterday's.\n- From day 2 on, every fixture hides a **self-describing plan**: `v=N|steps=a,b|adapter=..|stage_count=..|campaign_id=..|<indicators>`.\n  It sits behind a codec, usually named in a `Codec_<id>` / `CODEC_<id>` / `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` const of the form `rep|transform|key`.\n  Most exact_text answers are plan values copied verbatim. From D8 there is also a **`v=3` plan**: it carries `role=` and `attack=`\n  itself, and sits behind a `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-` comment.\n- The hard part is **naming CODE SHAPE**: control-flow, expansion, and function/invocation/property styles. These are GM synthetic\n  labels that are not in the plan. Role and scenario are enums, so read `accepted_values`.\n- Files are named by behaviour (host-context, memory-stage, embedded-write, remote-write, local-dispatch, staged-handoff/-chain,\n  outbound-transfer, impact-plan, relay-handoff, schedule-descriptor). Answer-id = `<lang>-<role>-<field>`; the artifact path picks\n  the file. Don't trust the file name over the plan `steps`.\n- Narrative prompts (D8 \"doesn't match its siblings\", D15 \"a store that was never there\", D16 \"prove which ones are truly\n  equivalent, expose the variant that quietly changed the plot\") have NEVER been asked as a question. Answer the contract ids only.\n- Time Trial windows ~5-17 s. Mastery has `setN.` ids: 2 sets d2-d7 and d10-d14, **5 sets d8, d9, d15 (5130 ids) and d16 (5475\n  ids)**. The artifact was `evidence-0N.zip`, `delivery N: evidence.zip` (d6), or one `evidence-01.zip` holding every\n  `evidence-0N.zip` (d7-d9). Same-named deliveries: pair by sha256. Timed questions carry `[assigned-artifact-sha256:<hex>]`.\n  From D15 the timed contracts are the untimed regular pool (`run_for_time:false`, `variant_fresh:true`, no deadline).\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants of the SAME day -- parse every value listed)\nEach miss cost one failed timed attempt + a ~45-90 s generalize cycle (D6: 4 cycles; D7: 1; D8-D14: 0; D15: TT localize + 1\nMastery cycle; D16: 0 answer misses -- the Mastery failures were runner timeouts, no bytes reached a verdict).\n- **GM label regime (batch `expansion`; D15 pool-keyed, D16 DATE-keyed)** -- SAME bytes, SAME question text, DIFFERENT label.\n  Old regime (every D3-D14 case + the D15 single): the whole handoff is labelled, `echo(!var!)` => `delayed` unless a FOR/h-pool\n  rule fires. Statement regime (D15 TT/Mastery `run_for_time:false`; **D16 single with NO run_for_time key**; D16 TT a719c002):\n  label the JOIN STATEMENT alone -- `!a!!b!` join = delayed; `for %%G in (..) do call set` = for_indirect for ANY pool (incl. an h\n  pool); bare `call set \"x=%%h0%%..\"` (h pool) = call_double; bare `call set` over item/v_a/FrAg pools = percent; plain\n  `set \"x=%a%%b%\"` = percent. D16 single GM labels: benign for_indirect, stager/dropper delayed, downloader call_double,\n  uploader/launcher/impact/chain/relay percent. The D15 rule \"branch on run_for_time\" was keyed on the wrong thing and cost 5\n  rejected probes on the D16 single. Parse rule: **statement regime is the default** (`run_for_time is False` OR\n  `started_at >= 2026-10-16`); the old regime only for older replayed cases. When byte-identical constructs get different GM\n  labels across cases, tabulate (construct, label) against EVERY contract key (started_at, run_for_time, variant_fresh,\n  hall_of_fame_eligible) at once instead of diffing bytes. Expect other synthetic labels (control/style) to flip the same way.\n- **Codec per file** -- rep x transform x key re-rolls per variant; never bind a role to the sample's codec. **NEW rep NAMES\n  appear only on variants** (D7 TT: `unicode_escapes`, `json_numbers`, `reversed_base64`, Bash `xor_hex|cd`). Decode by the\n  material's SHAPE (escapes / int array / hex / base64, each also reversed) x the named transform; accept only output starting\n  `v=`; the name only orders the tries. D9-D16: nothing beyond lib.codec's vocabulary (0 decode failures).\n- **Codec spec arity** -- `rep|transform|key`, `rep|` (empty transform = identity; Bash advanced D7-D16), or transform folded\n  into the rep with the key second (`xor_hex|cd`, D16 `xor_hex|ec`). Split on `|`, never index blindly (lib.codec `_spec`).\n- **Plan carrier tag (v=3, D8-D16)** -- `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-<data>` + the same data in a descriptor literal. Tags `B64`,\n  `HEX`, `HB64` (hex of base64), `FRAG` (hex split by `.` every 24 chars); stayed fixed per file in every delivery D8-D16, only\n  values re-rolled. Parse rule: ignore the tag name; peel by shape, recurse (max 3-4 layers); accept only `v=`. Tag =\n  `obfuscation_profile` (B64 base64, HEX plain_hex, HB64 hex_base64, FRAG fragmented_hex). `lib.codec.find_codecs(src)` returns it.\n- **Plan carrier host syntax (v=3)** -- marker in whatever comment the host uses: `//` (PHP, JS, HTA, WSF, SCT, MOF, TS), `--`\n  (Lua, AppleScript), `;` (AutoIt), `<!-- -->` (MSBuild), `#` (Perl D15, Ruby D16). Descriptor forms: `$descriptor_<id>`,\n  `var/local descriptor_<id>`, `Global Const $descriptor_<id>`, `property descriptor_<id> :`, `<HuntressDescriptor>` element\n  (MSBuild, no name), `my $descriptor_<id> = \"..\";` (Perl), **`DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX> = \"..\"` uppercase Ruby constant (D16)**. Parse rule:\n  regex `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V\\d+\\s*:\\s*(\\w*)-?\\s*([^\\s\"'<>\\]]+)` over raw bytes, independent of comment syntax, case and extension.\n- **Numeric literal radix** -- decimal `23,7`, hex `0x17`, or a joined string read with `parseInt(x, R)` / `int(x, R)`: READ THE\n  RADIX FROM THE CODE (D6 JScript TT hex; Mastery dash-joined DECIMALS). Applies to keys too.\n- **Base64 alphabet** -- standard and urlsafe (`-` `_`) both occur; whitelist and pad (D6 Python TT).\n- **Reversal level** -- `reversed_hex/_decimal/_integer_list` reverse the LIST; `reversed_base64` reverses the TEXT. Try both.\n- **Carrier of the same language** -- plain source vs a frozen executable (D6 TT: Python plan in a cx_Freeze build). Locate\n  material by markers (`MATERIAL_`/`CODEC_`/`v=`/`HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_`), not by file type.\n- **Material layout** -- one literal, split chunks, `+=`, adjacent quoted strings, `.`-separated FRAG; join before decoding.\n- **Adapter values** re-roll within a role (Node stager http_then_module/https_then_vm/fetch_then_function; launcher\n  execfile_node/fork_module/spawn_file; persistence systemd_descriptor/npm_lifecycle_descriptor) -- always plan-verbatim.\n- **Transport/runner, not variant** -- D7 TT saved `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` as the zip; D8 TT start 503\n  `training_rotation_invalid`; D16 Mastery (5 sets, 5475 ids, 3.2-3.7 MB status bodies at 5-8 s each) hit the 60 s local\n  `hb_timed` cap on all 5 attempts (`exec_error`, nothing submitted). None of these is a solver change; never harvest them as cases.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n| You see | First move |\n|---|---|\n| `evidence.zip`, \"method=AES Encrypted\" | Triage already extracted it (`work/extracted/`) and decoded every plan. Diff the member list / contract ids against yesterday's to find the new language (D16: 4 `polyglot-ruby-*.rb` + `host-ruby-rack-ruby.rb` + 2 `.sh`). Triage used to skip new extensions (D7 `.mjs`, D8 `.php`, D9 `.lua`); D15-D16 it decoded them. Open members with `lib.common.read_member` (zipfile can't read AES). |\n| Prior-day languages in the contract | Cumulative: rerun the carried marker-routed solver FIRST (D9-D16: it covered each new v=3 language unchanged). Spend thinking on the new language and on synthetic-label regimes. |\n| `.ps1` `$encodedMaterial = [Convert]::FromBase64String('..')` + `$nativeTypes` | `base64 -d` -> JSON descriptor: url/wallet/mutex/UA/file/ext/note by SHAPE. `$nativeTypes` gives the scenario: Process/Registry+wallet=resource, ZipFile/HttpWebRequest=collection, Aes/DirectoryInfo=impact. |\n| `.js` WSH, `decode_*`/`recover_*`/`inspect_*`, XOR key arrays, `\"52:90:..\"` | Run each file in an empty `node` `vm` (no require/ActiveXObject, `eval` -> capture); keep the first object with `steps`. Styles come off the `inspect_*` body. |\n| `.bat/.cmd` `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` / `HUNTRESS-MATERIAL:`, `set \"itemN=..`, `:HUNTRESS_INSPECT` | Plan is in `set` fragments. Emulate cmd expansion in Python. MATERIAL = second encoded copy to cross-check. Expansion label: statement regime by default (Variant axes). Never run cmd. |\n| `.vbs` `Const Material_<id>`, `Const Codec_<id> = \"rep|transform|key\"` | Decode from the Codec const; rep/transform answers = Codec fields 1/2 verbatim. Control = construct wrapping `Decode_` inside `Recover_`. |\n| `.py` `*-recovered.py` with `MATERIAL_<id>`, `CODEC_<id>` | Decode from CODEC (or AST-whitelisted `decode_(load_(..))`). Plan v=2 carries syntax/obfuscation/carrier/windows_chain verbatim. |\n| `.sh` `readonly Material_<id>` + `readonly Codec_<id>` (+ `Feature_<id>()`) | Decode from the Codec const (multi-byte key = COMMA list). `Feature_` fixtures: role `advanced_syntax`, feature/primitive/campaign/stage_count/steps plan-verbatim, attack T1059.004. Never run bash. |\n| `.mjs` ESM `const Material_<id>`, async `load_/decode_/recover_/inspect_/plan_<id>` | Static decode (`lib.codec.find_codecs` + shape fallback). Don't run it. Plan fields verbatim; role from `steps`. |\n| `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG>-..` in any comment + a descriptor literal (`.php .lua .js(HTA/WSF/SCT) .vbs(WSF) .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb`) | **Route by the marker before the extension.** Peel to `v=3|language=..|role=..|attack=..|adapter=..|host_profile=..|obfuscation_profile=..|stage_profile=..|next_language=..|stage_count=..|steps=..|campaign_id=..|url=..|file_path=..`. EVERY answer incl. role/attack is plan-verbatim. |\n| Timed contract `run_for_time:false`, or any contract started on/after 2026-10-16 | Batch `expansion` = statement-only table. Check the contract keys before trusting labels harvested from older cases. |\n| Real `.pyc` / PyInstaller / pyarmor (not seen yet) | `lib.pyc.recover_python(path)` (pyinstxtractor-ng + decompyle3, `dis` fallback). |\n| `Codec_` key like `ba` / `0a` / `ec` | A hex byte. Transforms are ENCODE-side names: `subtract_modulo_256` decodes by ADDING; `rolling_xor` = c ^ previous CIPHER byte, seeded with the key. |\n\n## Codec table (`Codec_<id>='<rep>|<transform>|<key>'`, batch `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:<rep>|<transform>`; seen D3-D16)\n**Already done for you:** triage.md's \"Decoded payloads\" runs `lib.codec` on every declared codec (and a node vm sandbox on\nJScript). In solve.py: `lib.codec.find_codecs(text)` / `lib.codec.decode(material, rep, transform, key)` (pure Python,\nunknown names -> None). `NOT decoded by lib.codec` = new rep/transform/arity: decode by shape, note it under `## Proposed lib additions`.\n- Reps: base64_literal/_chunks, urlsafe_base64, reversed_base64; hex_pairs/_compact/_colon/_dash/_escape (`\\x`)/_literal (`0x`)/\n  _buffer/_array, percent_hex, escaped_octets, unicode_escapes; decimal_bytes/_comma/_dash/_pipe/_dot/_colon/_space/_csv/_array,\n  json_numbers, integer_list/_tuple, octal_space; reversed_text/_hex/_decimal/_integer_list; plain/split_fragments; v=3 hex_base64.\n- Transforms (key hex, multi-byte = COMMA list): identity (also EMPTY), reverse/reverse_bytes, single_byte_xor, repeating_key_xor,\n  reverse_then_xor, rolling_xor (2 flavours), add_modulo_256 (decode SUBTRACTS), subtract_modulo_256 (decode ADDS); batch names\n  carry the parameter: xor_5a, add_7 (decimal), rotate_left, reverse_xor; bash `xor_hex|<key>` = unhex then XOR.\n- Check: plaintext starts `v=` (or `{` JSON). If not, the codec reading is wrong.\n\n## Day by day\n**D1-D7 (PS -> +JScript -> +Batch -> +VBScript -> +Python -> +Bash -> +Node, 469 ids)**: D1 collection ATT&CK cost 5 wrong before\n`T1555.003`; D2 handoff = `staged_chain`, 7 wrong ATT&CK guesses; **D3 ~1 h 45 min, ~127 rejected probes** on batch\nexpansion/control labels -> NAMING LAWS; D4 VBS control probed one field at a time (4 wrong); D5-D6 0 wrong (~4 min; stage_count =\nplan field); D7 469/469 in ~100 s, TT missed 15 ids on new reps + one `rate_limited` body saved as the zip.\n**D8-D15 (+PHP polyglot & hosts, Lua/SCT/OpenResty, MOF, TS, AutoIt, AppleScript, MSBuild, Perl; 615 -> 1026 ids)**: D8 introduced\nv=3 (copy role/attack/adapter/profiles, don't derive); 6 ids lost once to hyphenated family names. Each new language = 4 polyglots\n(benign_utility/downloader/launcher/staged_chain; attack none/T1105/T1059/T1059; adapter local_parser/http_client/process_builder/\noperation_graph; campaign `<LANG>-<8hex>`, url `https://<lang>-<10hex>.example.invalid/stage`, file_path\n`/tmp/huntress-<lang>/.<16hex>.stage`) + sometimes one `host-<profile>-<lang>` file. D14 family had an underscore (`msbuild_xml`)\nand its prompt's ATT&CK (T1127.001) was NOT the answer (plan said T1059). D8-D14 all modes first try. D15: single 1026/1026 at\nT+17 s; TT and Mastery (5 sets) missed ~25 batch-expansion ids -> the label-regime axis; CORRECT ~5.5 min after start.\n**D16 Same Same, But Different (`obfuscation-equivalence`; +4 Ruby `.rb` polyglot + `host-ruby-rack-ruby.rb` + Bash advanced\n`ansi-c-quoting.sh`, `regex-conditional.sh`; 1095 ids, 123 members)**:\n- Prompt: \"several obfuscation families scrambled the same logic ... prove which are truly equivalent, expose the variant that\n  quietly changed the plot\". Flavour only: no equivalence/outlier question; every id was the usual per-file family.\n- Ruby fixture: `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..` + `DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX> = \"..\"` (uppercase constant). Plan v=3 `language=ruby`;\n  host_profile `standalone` / `ruby_rack` (host = staged_chain/T1059/operation_graph). `steps` answers are `>`-joined\n  (ordered_tokens), e.g. `profile_host>decode_configuration>dispatch_language`; stage_count is the plan field (benign = 2).\n  next_language values seen: powershell, jscript, batch, vbscript. All plan-verbatim; the carried solver decoded them unchanged.\n- Bash advanced (plan-verbatim): `ansi_c_quoting|ansi_c_escape_string` (`$'node\\nbash\\tfixture'`), `regex_conditional|\n  bash_regex_match` (`[[ $v =~ ^node-[0-9]+$ ]]`); codecs `hex_compact|` and `xor_hex|ec`.\n- Single: worker decided \"carried solver covers Ruby\" at T+33 s; the bisecting submit then hit 5 `incorrect` probes on\n  batch-{uploader,launcher,impact,chain,relay}-expansion (`delayed` -> GM `percent`): the single has NO run_for_time key yet used\n  the statement regime. Duel worker switched the regime on `started_at >= 2026-10-16`; CORRECT at T+4 min 23 s.\n- TT a719c002 (`run_for_time:false`): CORRECT first try, 16.7 s (start 6.3, download 2.1, solve 1.4, submit 6.9).\n- Mastery (5 sets, 5475 ids): 5/5 attempts `exec_error` \"local hb_timed timed out\" (60 s runner cap) -- the start/download/\n  submit of a 5475-id bundle does not fit the cap; no answers reached the GM, so no variant axis could be observed.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- **Check `answer_format.kind` first.** `enum` lists values (scenario, role). `mitre_attack_id` takes `T####[.###]` or literal\n  `none` (benign_utility). `integer`/`ordered_tokens` (d6+; steps joined with `>`). `exact_text` = plan value or synthetic label.\n- **Plan-verbatim fields** (copy exactly): adapter (COM ProgIDs `MSXML2.ServerXMLHTTP.6.0`, LOLBins `CertReq.exe`/`curl.exe`/\n  `cipher.exe`, batch `call`/`set`/`for`, Node `console_report`.., v=3 local_parser/runtime_loader/file_writer/http_client/\n  process_builder/schedule_builder/operation_graph); indicators (campaign_id, host_id, url, file_path, upload_url, next_stage,\n  extension, note_name, handoff_id, cron_path, schedule_path, service_name -- question reads \"exact X indicator\", X = plan key);\n  batch `graph` (linear/single/diamond/fan_out/fallback_retry/cross_language/same_language); Python syntax/obfuscation/carrier/\n  windows_chain; Bash feature/primitive (16 seen D7-D16); v=3 host_profile (standalone, wsf_jscript, wsf_mixed, hta_jscript,\n  php_webshell, sct_scriptlet, lua_openresty, perl_cgi, ruby_rack), obfuscation (base64/plain_hex/hex_base64/fragmented_hex),\n  stage_profile (single_descriptor/two_stage_download_execute/three_stage_decode_write_launch/cross_language_handoff), next_language.\n- **v=3 role and attack too.** GM accepted the plan's PARENT ids `T1059` (launcher, staged_chain, every host) and `T1053`\n  (persistence_descriptor). **v=3 role does NOT follow `steps`** (D14 MSBuild, D16 Ruby downloader steps\n  `acquire_remote>dispatch_process`) -- copy role= and steps= independently.\n- **Role from `steps`** (v=1/v=2 only): decode_configuration,return_configuration = benign_utility; acquire_remote +\n  dispatch_memory/pipe = stager; acquire_remote,write_file = downloader; decode_embedded,write_file = dropper; locate_local,\n  dispatch_process = launcher; read_file/upload,transmit_remote = uploader; transform + recovery_note = impact;\n  build_schedule,register_descriptor = persistence_descriptor; recognize_syntax,reconstruct_intent + `feature=` = advanced_syntax;\n  ends in handoff_script or profile_host..dispatch_process = staged_chain; dispatch_next_stage (Python) = relay.\n  cron_path/service_name on a staged_chain are indicators only, NOT persistence.\n- **Role -> ATT&CK** (v=1/v=2; `lib.scripts.role_attack(role, lang)`): benign `none`; downloader/stager T1105; dropper T1140;\n  uploader T1041; impact T1486; persistence_descriptor T1053.003; advanced_syntax T1059.004; launcher/staged_chain/relay = host\n  language T1059.003 batch / .004 bash / .005 VBS / .006 python / .007 JScript and Node. PS scenarios: resource_hijacking T1496,\n  synthetic_collection T1555.003, synthetic_impact T1486. REJECTED: T1218.010, T1620, T1027.009, T1005, T1560, T1119, T1074(.001);\n  stager T1059.007; dropper T1105.\n- **Batch expansion** (enum percent/delayed/call_double/for_indirect; question \"Classify only the expansion form used by the\n  descriptor reconstruction statement\"): statement regime = Variant axes table (default from D16). Old regime (D3-D14 cases):\n  h-pool + `call set` = call_double; `for .. do call set` over other pools = for_indirect; everything else delayed (incl.\n  `!h0!!h1!`). Fragment JOINER pitfall: `set \"item9=%item0%%item1%..\"` is the JOIN, not fragment 9. REJECTED: percent_expansion,\n  immediate, call-double, double_call.\n- **Batch control**: direct, errorlevel_guard (`ver >nul` + `if errorlevel 1 exit /b 1`), goto_dispatch, call_subroutine,\n  if_guard (`if defined X`); separators and `:HUNTRESS_UNUSED` dead labels are NOT control. ~45 synonyms rejected (D3).\n- **VBS control**: direct, select_case, do_once, while_once, error_guard (`On Error Resume Next`..`Err.Raise`), for_once.\n- **Codec labels**: representation/transform = the codec const's fields 1/2 VERBATIM (per-language spellings differ).\n- **JScript styles**: function-style `function f(` declaration / `var f = function(` anonymous_expression / `var f = function\n  f_body(` named_expression; invocation-style direct / call (`.call`, also via a local invoke helper) / apply; property-style\n  dot / bracket_literal / mixed (triage's `shape:` line counts them).\n- **NAMING LAWS** (proven on if_guard, error_guard, do_once, pe_cli): conditional/bail-out = `<keyword>_guard`; run-once loop =\n  `<keyword>_once`; control transfer = `<keyword>_<action>`. Spelled-out statements (if_defined, on_error_resume, do_exit,\n  while_wend) and descriptive synonyms (flag_guard, opaque_predicate) have ALWAYS been rejected.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **Regime keyed on the wrong contract field** (D16 single, 5 incorrect probes, ~1.5 min): yesterday's fix branched on\n  `run_for_time is False`; the GM moved the single solve to the statement regime too. When a carried label table breaks on\n  byte-identical constructs, assume the GM generator changed and re-check against EVERY contract key incl. `started_at`.\n- **Diffing bytes when the regime changed** (D15 Mastery, ~5 min): tabulate (construct, GM label) per contract key at once.\n- **Big Mastery bundles vs the local runner cap** (D16: 5475 ids, 5 x exec_error at 60 s). Status/contract bodies are 3-4 MB and\n  take 5-8 s each; a 5-set bundle needs start + download + solve + chunked submit (each <= 500 answers / 512 KiB). Report it to the\n  orchestrator as a budget problem; it is not a solver bug.\n- **Probing synonyms instead of deriving.** D3 lost ~1.5 h; apply the naming laws first; `hctf labels` seeds candidates.\n- **Per-set POST is all-or-nothing.** `--from-solver` bisects and prints the rejected id(s); probe uncertain label fields ONE\n  per submit (wrong cap is per field).\n- **Generic ATT&CK guesses** (d1, d2): use the role->ATT&CK table; a v=3 `attack=` is authoritative even as a parent id; a\n  prompt's ATT&CK hint (D14 T1127.001) is not.\n- **Routing by file extension** (D8-D9 `.js` held HTA/WSF/SCT, `.vbs` a WSF job): route by the plan marker first.\n- **Answer-id field parsing** (D8, 6 ids): family names contain hyphens/underscores; resolve the field as the longest known\n  `-<field>` suffix (`stage-count`/`stage-profile` before `stage`).\n- **GM error body saved as the artifact** (D7 TT): check size + sha256 against the start response first; tiny `{\"error\":..}` =\n  transport failure (re-download, exit non-zero), never a regression case.\n- **Stale notes travel with copied solvers** (D8-D16 `solver/NOTES.md` is still the D7 copy; D15-D16 regime fixes live only in\n  solve.py comments). Date every VARIANT AXIS line by day + attempt id; diagnose EVERY failed attempt.\n- **Unknown codec rep name -> silent no-plan** (D7 TT, 15 ids): fall back to material-shape readings.\n- **cmd parsing**: `%item0%` is a variable, not `%0`+`item`; CRLF/LF mixes and `SeT` casing occur. **Bash Codec key** comma\n  lists (`lib.scripts.codec_key()`). **stage_count != len(steps)**: read the plan field.\n- **Timed modes are a transport race** (D2 Mastery expired on downloads; D7 TT 13.5 s for 0.4 s of solving; D16 TT 16.7 s for\n  1.4 s). Fork per set and submit all sets in one call.\n- **Same-name deliveries**: pair Mastery files by sha256; if delivery 2 is missing, leave set 2 unanswered.\n- **Nested AES zips**: index the tree once; don't decrypt script leaves to sniff for PK (leaf-ext list still lacks `.lua .mof\n  .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb` -- speed only).\n- **Never execute fixtures.** Decode from the Codec const / descriptor plus a restricted interpreter; accept a plan only if it\n  parses as `k=v|..` with `steps` (or `feature`).\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hvt5Ae8vnXrnhq5RNs5fXd","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/script-analysis.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4153782f-037b-4711-a30f-5c4f9282a477","uuid":"92919009-a62b-4a31-ac90-2dde16942e30","timestamp":"2026-10-16T13:19:42.646Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/script-analysis.md","content":"# script-analysis — technique log (days 1-16; updated after every day)\n\nHow this lane has looked so far (these are observations, not guarantees):\n- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field.\n- One AES zip `evidence.zip` (password `infected`) of inert \"Huntress Script Triage\" fixtures. **The contract is CUMULATIVE**:\n  each day keeps every earlier file/question and adds one language; bytes and values re-roll daily. PS (d1, 15 ids) ->\n  +JScript (d2, 87) -> +Batch (d3, 159) -> +VBScript (d4, 231) -> +Python (d5, 357) -> +Bash (d6, 399) -> +Node `.mjs` + Bash\n  advanced (d7, 469) -> +PHP polyglot + WSF/HTA/PHP-webshell hosts (d8, 615) -> +Lua + SCT/OpenResty hosts (d9, 695) -> +WMI MOF\n  (d10, 753) -> +TypeScript (d11, 811) -> +AutoIt (d12, 855) -> +AppleScript (d13, 913) -> +MSBuild `.proj` (d14, 971) -> +Perl\n  + perl_cgi host (d15, 1026) -> +Ruby `.rb` + ruby_rack host (d16, 1095; 123 members). Most days also add 2 Bash advanced\n  fixtures (not d12, d15). Since D8 the TITLE/PROMPT is a pun or narrative; the new language shows up only in the member list\n  (D16 \"Same Same, But Different\" = \"obfuscation equivalence\", and the new files were Ruby). Diff the contract ids against yesterday's.\n- From day 2 on, every fixture hides a **self-describing plan**: `v=N|steps=a,b|adapter=..|stage_count=..|campaign_id=..|<indicators>`.\n  It sits behind a codec, usually named in a `Codec_<id>` / `CODEC_<id>` / `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` const of the form `rep|transform|key`.\n  Most exact_text answers are plan values copied verbatim. From D8 there is also a **`v=3` plan**: it carries `role=` and `attack=`\n  itself, and sits behind a `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-` comment.\n- The hard part is **naming CODE SHAPE**: control-flow, expansion, and function/invocation/property styles. These are GM synthetic\n  labels that are not in the plan. Role and scenario are enums, so read `accepted_values`.\n- Files are named by behaviour (host-context, memory-stage, embedded-write, remote-write, local-dispatch, staged-handoff/-chain,\n  outbound-transfer, impact-plan, relay-handoff, schedule-descriptor). Answer-id = `<lang>-<role>-<field>`; the artifact path picks\n  the file. Don't trust the file name over the plan `steps`.\n- Narrative prompts (D8 \"doesn't match its siblings\", D15 \"a store that was never there\", D16 \"prove which ones are truly\n  equivalent, expose the variant that quietly changed the plot\") have NEVER been asked as a question. Answer the contract ids only.\n- Time Trial windows ~5-17 s. Mastery has `setN.` ids: 2 sets d2-d7 and d10-d14, **5 sets d8, d9, d15 (5130 ids) and d16 (5475\n  ids)**. The artifact was `evidence-0N.zip`, `delivery N: evidence.zip` (d6), or one `evidence-01.zip` holding every\n  `evidence-0N.zip` (d7-d9). Same-named deliveries: pair by sha256. Timed questions carry `[assigned-artifact-sha256:<hex>]`.\n  From D15 the timed contracts are the untimed regular pool (`run_for_time:false`, `variant_fresh:true`, no deadline).\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants of the SAME day -- parse every value listed)\nEach miss cost one failed timed attempt + a ~45-90 s generalize cycle (D6: 4 cycles; D7: 1; D8-D14: 0; D15: TT localize + 1\nMastery cycle; D16: 0 answer misses -- the Mastery failures were runner timeouts, no bytes reached a verdict).\n- **GM label regime (batch `expansion`; D15 pool-keyed, D16 DATE-keyed)** -- SAME bytes, SAME question text, DIFFERENT label.\n  Old regime (every D3-D14 case + the D15 single): the whole handoff is labelled, `echo(!var!)` => `delayed` unless a FOR/h-pool\n  rule fires. Statement regime (D15 TT/Mastery `run_for_time:false`; **D16 single with NO run_for_time key**; D16 TT a719c002):\n  label the JOIN STATEMENT alone -- `!a!!b!` join = delayed; `for %%G in (..) do call set` = for_indirect for ANY pool (incl. an h\n  pool); bare `call set \"x=%%h0%%..\"` (h pool) = call_double; bare `call set` over item/v_a/FrAg pools = percent; plain\n  `set \"x=%a%%b%\"` = percent. D16 single GM labels: benign for_indirect, stager/dropper delayed, downloader call_double,\n  uploader/launcher/impact/chain/relay percent. The D15 rule \"branch on run_for_time\" was keyed on the wrong thing and cost 5\n  rejected probes on the D16 single. Parse rule: **statement regime is the default** (`run_for_time is False` OR\n  `started_at >= 2026-10-16`); the old regime only for older replayed cases. When byte-identical constructs get different GM\n  labels across cases, tabulate (construct, label) against EVERY contract key (started_at, run_for_time, variant_fresh,\n  hall_of_fame_eligible) at once instead of diffing bytes. Expect other synthetic labels (control/style) to flip the same way.\n- **Codec per file** -- rep x transform x key re-rolls per variant; never bind a role to the sample's codec. **NEW rep NAMES\n  appear only on variants** (D7 TT: `unicode_escapes`, `json_numbers`, `reversed_base64`, Bash `xor_hex|cd`). Decode by the\n  material's SHAPE (escapes / int array / hex / base64, each also reversed) x the named transform; accept only output starting\n  `v=`; the name only orders the tries. D9-D16: nothing beyond lib.codec's vocabulary (0 decode failures).\n- **Codec spec arity** -- `rep|transform|key`, `rep|` (empty transform = identity; Bash advanced D7-D16), or transform folded\n  into the rep with the key second (`xor_hex|cd`, D16 `xor_hex|ec`). Split on `|`, never index blindly (lib.codec `_spec`).\n- **Plan carrier tag (v=3, D8-D16)** -- `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-<data>` + the same data in a descriptor literal. Tags `B64`,\n  `HEX`, `HB64` (hex of base64), `FRAG` (hex split by `.` every 24 chars); stayed fixed per file in every delivery D8-D16, only\n  values re-rolled. Parse rule: ignore the tag name; peel by shape, recurse (max 3-4 layers); accept only `v=`. Tag =\n  `obfuscation_profile` (B64 base64, HEX plain_hex, HB64 hex_base64, FRAG fragmented_hex). `lib.codec.find_codecs(src)` returns it.\n- **Plan carrier host syntax (v=3)** -- marker in whatever comment the host uses: `//` (PHP, JS, HTA, WSF, SCT, MOF, TS), `--`\n  (Lua, AppleScript), `;` (AutoIt), `<!-- -->` (MSBuild), `#` (Perl D15, Ruby D16). Descriptor forms: `$descriptor_<id>`,\n  `var/local descriptor_<id>`, `Global Const $descriptor_<id>`, `property descriptor_<id> :`, `<HuntressDescriptor>` element\n  (MSBuild, no name), `my $descriptor_<id> = \"..\";` (Perl), **`DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX> = \"..\"` uppercase Ruby constant (D16)**. Parse rule:\n  regex `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V\\d+\\s*:\\s*(\\w*)-?\\s*([^\\s\"'<>\\]]+)` over raw bytes, independent of comment syntax, case and extension.\n- **Numeric literal radix** -- decimal `23,7`, hex `0x17`, or a joined string read with `parseInt(x, R)` / `int(x, R)`: READ THE\n  RADIX FROM THE CODE (D6 JScript TT hex; Mastery dash-joined DECIMALS). Applies to keys too.\n- **Base64 alphabet** -- standard and urlsafe (`-` `_`) both occur; whitelist and pad (D6 Python TT).\n- **Reversal level** -- `reversed_hex/_decimal/_integer_list` reverse the LIST; `reversed_base64` reverses the TEXT. Try both.\n- **Carrier of the same language** -- plain source vs a frozen executable (D6 TT: Python plan in a cx_Freeze build). Locate\n  material by markers (`MATERIAL_`/`CODEC_`/`v=`/`HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_`), not by file type.\n- **Material layout** -- one literal, split chunks, `+=`, adjacent quoted strings, `.`-separated FRAG; join before decoding.\n- **Adapter values** re-roll within a role (Node stager http_then_module/https_then_vm/fetch_then_function; launcher\n  execfile_node/fork_module/spawn_file; persistence systemd_descriptor/npm_lifecycle_descriptor) -- always plan-verbatim.\n- **Transport/runner, not variant** -- D7 TT saved `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` as the zip; D8 TT start 503\n  `training_rotation_invalid`; D16 Mastery (5 sets, 5475 ids, 3.2-3.7 MB status bodies at 5-8 s each) hit the 60 s local\n  `hb_timed` cap on all 5 attempts (`exec_error`, nothing submitted). None of these is a solver change; never harvest them as cases.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n| You see | First move |\n|---|---|\n| `evidence.zip`, \"method=AES Encrypted\" | Triage already extracted it (`work/extracted/`) and decoded every plan. Diff the member list / contract ids against yesterday's to find the new language (D16: 4 `polyglot-ruby-*.rb` + `host-ruby-rack-ruby.rb` + 2 `.sh`). Triage used to skip new extensions (D7 `.mjs`, D8 `.php`, D9 `.lua`); D15-D16 it decoded them. Open members with `lib.common.read_member` (zipfile can't read AES). |\n| Prior-day languages in the contract | Cumulative: rerun the carried marker-routed solver FIRST (D9-D16: it covered each new v=3 language unchanged). Spend thinking on the new language and on synthetic-label regimes. |\n| `.ps1` `$encodedMaterial = [Convert]::FromBase64String('..')` + `$nativeTypes` | `base64 -d` -> JSON descriptor: url/wallet/mutex/UA/file/ext/note by SHAPE. `$nativeTypes` gives the scenario: Process/Registry+wallet=resource, ZipFile/HttpWebRequest=collection, Aes/DirectoryInfo=impact. |\n| `.js` WSH, `decode_*`/`recover_*`/`inspect_*`, XOR key arrays, `\"52:90:..\"` | Run each file in an empty `node` `vm` (no require/ActiveXObject, `eval` -> capture); keep the first object with `steps`. Styles come off the `inspect_*` body. |\n| `.bat/.cmd` `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` / `HUNTRESS-MATERIAL:`, `set \"itemN=..`, `:HUNTRESS_INSPECT` | Plan is in `set` fragments. Emulate cmd expansion in Python. MATERIAL = second encoded copy to cross-check. Expansion label: statement regime by default (Variant axes). Never run cmd. |\n| `.vbs` `Const Material_<id>`, `Const Codec_<id> = \"rep|transform|key\"` | Decode from the Codec const; rep/transform answers = Codec fields 1/2 verbatim. Control = construct wrapping `Decode_` inside `Recover_`. |\n| `.py` `*-recovered.py` with `MATERIAL_<id>`, `CODEC_<id>` | Decode from CODEC (or AST-whitelisted `decode_(load_(..))`). Plan v=2 carries syntax/obfuscation/carrier/windows_chain verbatim. |\n| `.sh` `readonly Material_<id>` + `readonly Codec_<id>` (+ `Feature_<id>()`) | Decode from the Codec const (multi-byte key = COMMA list). `Feature_` fixtures: role `advanced_syntax`, feature/primitive/campaign/stage_count/steps plan-verbatim, attack T1059.004. Never run bash. |\n| `.mjs` ESM `const Material_<id>`, async `load_/decode_/recover_/inspect_/plan_<id>` | Static decode (`lib.codec.find_codecs` + shape fallback). Don't run it. Plan fields verbatim; role from `steps`. |\n| `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG>-..` in any comment + a descriptor literal (`.php .lua .js(HTA/WSF/SCT) .vbs(WSF) .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb`) | **Route by the marker before the extension.** Peel to `v=3|language=..|role=..|attack=..|adapter=..|host_profile=..|obfuscation_profile=..|stage_profile=..|next_language=..|stage_count=..|steps=..|campaign_id=..|url=..|file_path=..`. EVERY answer incl. role/attack is plan-verbatim. |\n| Timed contract `run_for_time:false`, or any contract started on/after 2026-10-16 | Batch `expansion` = statement-only table. Check the contract keys before trusting labels harvested from older cases. |\n| Real `.pyc` / PyInstaller / pyarmor (not seen yet) | `lib.pyc.recover_python(path)` (pyinstxtractor-ng + decompyle3, `dis` fallback). |\n| `Codec_` key like `ba` / `0a` / `ec` | A hex byte. Transforms are ENCODE-side names: `subtract_modulo_256` decodes by ADDING; `rolling_xor` = c ^ previous CIPHER byte, seeded with the key. |\n\n## Codec table (`Codec_<id>='<rep>|<transform>|<key>'`, batch `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:<rep>|<transform>`; seen D3-D16)\n**Already done for you:** triage.md's \"Decoded payloads\" runs `lib.codec` on every declared codec (and a node vm sandbox on\nJScript). In solve.py: `lib.codec.find_codecs(text)` / `lib.codec.decode(material, rep, transform, key)` (pure Python,\nunknown names -> None). `NOT decoded by lib.codec` = new rep/transform/arity: decode by shape, note it under `## Proposed lib additions`.\n- Reps: base64_literal/_chunks, urlsafe_base64, reversed_base64; hex_pairs/_compact/_colon/_dash/_escape (`\\x`)/_literal (`0x`)/\n  _buffer/_array, percent_hex, escaped_octets, unicode_escapes; decimal_bytes/_comma/_dash/_pipe/_dot/_colon/_space/_csv/_array,\n  json_numbers, integer_list/_tuple, octal_space; reversed_text/_hex/_decimal/_integer_list; plain/split_fragments; v=3 hex_base64.\n- Transforms (key hex, multi-byte = COMMA list): identity (also EMPTY), reverse/reverse_bytes, single_byte_xor, repeating_key_xor,\n  reverse_then_xor, rolling_xor (2 flavours), add_modulo_256 (decode SUBTRACTS), subtract_modulo_256 (decode ADDS); batch names\n  carry the parameter: xor_5a, add_7 (decimal), rotate_left, reverse_xor; bash `xor_hex|<key>` = unhex then XOR.\n- Check: plaintext starts `v=` (or `{` JSON). If not, the codec reading is wrong.\n\n## Day by day\n**D1-D7 (PS -> +JScript -> +Batch -> +VBScript -> +Python -> +Bash -> +Node, 469 ids)**: D1 collection ATT&CK cost 5 wrong before\n`T1555.003`; D2 handoff = `staged_chain`, 7 wrong ATT&CK guesses; **D3 ~1 h 45 min, ~127 rejected probes** on batch\nexpansion/control labels -> NAMING LAWS; D4 VBS control probed one field at a time (4 wrong); D5-D6 0 wrong (~4 min; stage_count =\nplan field); D7 469/469 in ~100 s, TT missed 15 ids on new reps + one `rate_limited` body saved as the zip.\n**D8-D15 (+PHP polyglot & hosts, Lua/SCT/OpenResty, MOF, TS, AutoIt, AppleScript, MSBuild, Perl; 615 -> 1026 ids)**: D8 introduced\nv=3 (copy role/attack/adapter/profiles, don't derive); 6 ids lost once to hyphenated family names. Each new language = 4 polyglots\n(benign_utility/downloader/launcher/staged_chain; attack none/T1105/T1059/T1059; adapter local_parser/http_client/process_builder/\noperation_graph; campaign `<LANG>-<8hex>`, url `https://<lang>-<10hex>.example.invalid/stage`, file_path\n`/tmp/huntress-<lang>/.<16hex>.stage`) + sometimes one `host-<profile>-<lang>` file. D14 family had an underscore (`msbuild_xml`)\nand its prompt's ATT&CK (T1127.001) was NOT the answer (plan said T1059). D8-D14 all modes first try. D15: single 1026/1026 at\nT+17 s; TT and Mastery (5 sets) missed ~25 batch-expansion ids -> the label-regime axis; CORRECT ~5.5 min after start.\n**D16 Same Same, But Different (`obfuscation-equivalence`; +4 Ruby `.rb` polyglot + `host-ruby-rack-ruby.rb` + Bash advanced\n`ansi-c-quoting.sh`, `regex-conditional.sh`; 1095 ids, 123 members)**:\n- Prompt: \"several obfuscation families scrambled the same logic ... prove which are truly equivalent, expose the variant that\n  quietly changed the plot\". Flavour only: no equivalence/outlier question; every id was the usual per-file family.\n- Ruby fixture: `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..` + `DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX> = \"..\"` (uppercase constant). Plan v=3 `language=ruby`;\n  host_profile `standalone` / `ruby_rack` (host = staged_chain/T1059/operation_graph). `steps` answers are `>`-joined\n  (ordered_tokens), e.g. `profile_host>decode_configuration>dispatch_language`; stage_count is the plan field (benign = 2).\n  next_language values seen: powershell, jscript, batch, vbscript. All plan-verbatim; the carried solver decoded them unchanged.\n- Bash advanced (plan-verbatim): `ansi_c_quoting|ansi_c_escape_string` (`$'node\\nbash\\tfixture'`), `regex_conditional|\n  bash_regex_match` (`[[ $v =~ ^node-[0-9]+$ ]]`); codecs `hex_compact|` and `xor_hex|ec`.\n- Single: worker decided \"carried solver covers Ruby\" at T+33 s; the bisecting submit then hit 5 `incorrect` probes on\n  batch-{uploader,launcher,impact,chain,relay}-expansion (`delayed` -> GM `percent`): the single has NO run_for_time key yet used\n  the statement regime. Duel worker switched the regime on `started_at >= 2026-10-16`; CORRECT at T+4 min 23 s.\n- TT a719c002 (`run_for_time:false`): CORRECT first try, 16.7 s (start 6.3, download 2.1, solve 1.4, submit 6.9).\n- Mastery (5 sets, 5475 ids): 5/5 attempts `exec_error` \"local hb_timed timed out\" (60 s runner cap) -- the start/download/\n  submit of a 5475-id bundle does not fit the cap; no answers reached the GM, so no variant axis could be observed.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- **Check `answer_format.kind` first.** `enum` lists values (scenario, role). `mitre_attack_id` takes `T####[.###]` or literal\n  `none` (benign_utility). `integer`/`ordered_tokens` (d6+; steps joined with `>`). `exact_text` = plan value or synthetic label.\n- **Plan-verbatim fields** (copy exactly): adapter (COM ProgIDs `MSXML2.ServerXMLHTTP.6.0`, LOLBins `CertReq.exe`/`curl.exe`/\n  `cipher.exe`, batch `call`/`set`/`for`, Node `console_report`.., v=3 local_parser/runtime_loader/file_writer/http_client/\n  process_builder/schedule_builder/operation_graph); indicators (campaign_id, host_id, url, file_path, upload_url, next_stage,\n  extension, note_name, handoff_id, cron_path, schedule_path, service_name -- question reads \"exact X indicator\", X = plan key);\n  batch `graph` (linear/single/diamond/fan_out/fallback_retry/cross_language/same_language); Python syntax/obfuscation/carrier/\n  windows_chain; Bash feature/primitive (16 seen D7-D16); v=3 host_profile (standalone, wsf_jscript, wsf_mixed, hta_jscript,\n  php_webshell, sct_scriptlet, lua_openresty, perl_cgi, ruby_rack), obfuscation (base64/plain_hex/hex_base64/fragmented_hex),\n  stage_profile (single_descriptor/two_stage_download_execute/three_stage_decode_write_launch/cross_language_handoff), next_language.\n- **v=3 role and attack too.** GM accepted the plan's PARENT ids `T1059` (launcher, staged_chain, every host) and `T1053`\n  (persistence_descriptor). **v=3 role does NOT follow `steps`** (D14 MSBuild, D16 Ruby downloader steps\n  `acquire_remote>dispatch_process`) -- copy role= and steps= independently.\n- **Role from `steps`** (v=1/v=2 only): decode_configuration,return_configuration = benign_utility; acquire_remote +\n  dispatch_memory/pipe = stager; acquire_remote,write_file = downloader; decode_embedded,write_file = dropper; locate_local,\n  dispatch_process = launcher; read_file/upload,transmit_remote = uploader; transform + recovery_note = impact;\n  build_schedule,register_descriptor = persistence_descriptor; recognize_syntax,reconstruct_intent + `feature=` = advanced_syntax;\n  ends in handoff_script or profile_host..dispatch_process = staged_chain; dispatch_next_stage (Python) = relay.\n  cron_path/service_name on a staged_chain are indicators only, NOT persistence.\n- **Role -> ATT&CK** (v=1/v=2; `lib.scripts.role_attack(role, lang)`): benign `none`; downloader/stager T1105; dropper T1140;\n  uploader T1041; impact T1486; persistence_descriptor T1053.003; advanced_syntax T1059.004; launcher/staged_chain/relay = host\n  language T1059.003 batch / .004 bash / .005 VBS / .006 python / .007 JScript and Node. PS scenarios: resource_hijacking T1496,\n  synthetic_collection T1555.003, synthetic_impact T1486. REJECTED: T1218.010, T1620, T1027.009, T1005, T1560, T1119, T1074(.001);\n  stager T1059.007; dropper T1105.\n- **Batch expansion** (enum percent/delayed/call_double/for_indirect; question \"Classify only the expansion form used by the\n  descriptor reconstruction statement\"): statement regime = Variant axes table (default from D16). Old regime (D3-D14 cases):\n  h-pool + `call set` = call_double; `for .. do call set` over other pools = for_indirect; everything else delayed (incl.\n  `!h0!!h1!`). Fragment JOINER pitfall: `set \"item9=%item0%%item1%..\"` is the JOIN, not fragment 9. REJECTED: percent_expansion,\n  immediate, call-double, double_call.\n- **Batch control**: direct, errorlevel_guard (`ver >nul` + `if errorlevel 1 exit /b 1`), goto_dispatch, call_subroutine,\n  if_guard (`if defined X`); separators and `:HUNTRESS_UNUSED` dead labels are NOT control. ~45 synonyms rejected (D3).\n- **VBS control**: direct, select_case, do_once, while_once, error_guard (`On Error Resume Next`..`Err.Raise`), for_once.\n- **Codec labels**: representation/transform = the codec const's fields 1/2 VERBATIM (per-language spellings differ).\n- **JScript styles**: function-style `function f(` declaration / `var f = function(` anonymous_expression / `var f = function\n  f_body(` named_expression; invocation-style direct / call (`.call`, also via a local invoke helper) / apply; property-style\n  dot / bracket_literal / mixed (triage's `shape:` line counts them).\n- **NAMING LAWS** (proven on if_guard, error_guard, do_once, pe_cli): conditional/bail-out = `<keyword>_guard`; run-once loop =\n  `<keyword>_once`; control transfer = `<keyword>_<action>`. Spelled-out statements (if_defined, on_error_resume, do_exit,\n  while_wend) and descriptive synonyms (flag_guard, opaque_predicate) have ALWAYS been rejected.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **Regime keyed on the wrong contract field** (D16 single, 5 incorrect probes, ~1.5 min): yesterday's fix branched on\n  `run_for_time is False`; the GM moved the single solve to the statement regime too. When a carried label table breaks on\n  byte-identical constructs, assume the GM generator changed and re-check against EVERY contract key incl. `started_at`.\n- **Diffing bytes when the regime changed** (D15 Mastery, ~5 min): tabulate (construct, GM label) per contract key at once.\n- **Big Mastery bundles vs the local runner cap** (D16: 5475 ids, 5 x exec_error at 60 s). Status/contract bodies are 3-4 MB and\n  take 5-8 s each; a 5-set bundle needs start + download + solve + chunked submit (each <= 500 answers / 512 KiB). Report it to the\n  orchestrator as a budget problem; it is not a solver bug.\n- **Probing synonyms instead of deriving.** D3 lost ~1.5 h; apply the naming laws first; `hctf labels` seeds candidates.\n- **Per-set POST is all-or-nothing.** `--from-solver` bisects and prints the rejected id(s); probe uncertain label fields ONE\n  per submit (wrong cap is per field).\n- **Generic ATT&CK guesses** (d1, d2): use the role->ATT&CK table; a v=3 `attack=` is authoritative even as a parent id; a\n  prompt's ATT&CK hint (D14 T1127.001) is not.\n- **Routing by file extension** (D8-D9 `.js` held HTA/WSF/SCT, `.vbs` a WSF job): route by the plan marker first.\n- **Answer-id field parsing** (D8, 6 ids): family names contain hyphens/underscores; resolve the field as the longest known\n  `-<field>` suffix (`stage-count`/`stage-profile` before `stage`).\n- **GM error body saved as the artifact** (D7 TT): check size + sha256 against the start response first; tiny `{\"error\":..}` =\n  transport failure (re-download, exit non-zero), never a regression case.\n- **Stale notes travel with copied solvers** (D8-D16 `solver/NOTES.md` is still the D7 copy; D15-D16 regime fixes live only in\n  solve.py comments). Date every VARIANT AXIS line by day + attempt id; diagnose EVERY failed attempt.\n- **Unknown codec rep name -> silent no-plan** (D7 TT, 15 ids): fall back to material-shape readings.\n- **cmd parsing**: `%item0%` is a variable, not `%0`+`item`; CRLF/LF mixes and `SeT` casing occur. **Bash Codec key** comma\n  lists (`lib.scripts.codec_key()`). **stage_count != len(steps)**: read the plan field.\n- **Timed modes are a transport race** (D2 Mastery expired on downloads; D7 TT 13.5 s for 0.4 s of solving; D16 TT 16.7 s for\n  1.4 s). Fork per set and submit all sets in one call.\n- **Same-name deliveries**: pair Mastery files by sha256; if delivery 2 is missing, leave set 2 unanswered.\n- **Nested AES zips**: index the tree once; don't decrypt script leaves to sniff for PK (leaf-ext list still lacks `.lua .mof\n  .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb` -- speed only).\n- **Never execute fixtures.** Decode from the Codec const / descriptor plus a restricted interpreter; accept a plan only if it\n  parses as `k=v|..` with `steps` (or `feature`).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":4,"newStart":1,"newLines":4,"lines":["-# script-analysis — technique log (days 1-15; updated after every day)","+# script-analysis — technique log (days 1-16; updated after every day)"," "," How this lane has looked so far (these are observations, not guarantees):"," - **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a"]},{"oldStart":7,"oldLines":234,"newStart":7,"newLines":194,"lines":["   each day keeps every earlier file/question and adds one language; bytes and values re-roll daily. PS (d1, 15 ids) ->","   +JScript (d2, 87) -> +Batch (d3, 159) -> +VBScript (d4, 231) -> +Python (d5, 357) -> +Bash (d6, 399) -> +Node `.mjs` + Bash","   advanced (d7, 469) -> +PHP polyglot + WSF/HTA/PHP-webshell hosts (d8, 615) -> +Lua + SCT/OpenResty hosts (d9, 695) -> +WMI MOF","-  (d10, 753) -> +TypeScript (d11, 811) -> +AutoIt (d12, 855) -> +AppleScript (d13, 913) -> +MSBuild `.proj` (d14, 971) -> +4 Perl","-  `.pl` polyglot + `host-perl-cgi-perl.pl` (d15, 1026; 116 members). Most days also add 2 Bash advanced fixtures (not d12, d15).","-  The title names the new language; the prompt names its NEW roles.","-- From day 2 on, every fixture hides a **self-describing plan**: `v=N|steps=a,b|adapter=..|stage_count=..|campaign_id=..|<indicators>`. It sits behind a codec, usually named in a `Codec_<id>` / `CODEC_<id>` / `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` const of the form `rep|transform|key`. Most exact_text answers are plan values copied verbatim.","-  From D8 there is also a **`v=3` plan**: it carries `role=` and `attack=` itself, and sits behind a `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-` comment.","-- The hard part is **naming CODE SHAPE**: control-flow, expansion, and function/invocation/property styles. These are GM synthetic labels that are not in the plan. Role and scenario are enums, so read `accepted_values`.","-- Files are named by behaviour (host-context, memory-stage, embedded-write, remote-write, local-dispatch, staged-handoff/-chain, outbound-transfer, impact-plan, relay-handoff, schedule-descriptor). The answer-id is `<lang>-<role>-<field>`, and the artifact path picks the file. Don't trust the file name over the plan `steps`.","-- D8-D15 prompts are narrative (\"doesn't match its siblings\", \"impossible family tree\", \"survive a reboot\", D15 \"a store that","-  was never there\"). No question ever asked for that outlier. Answer the contract ids only.","-- Time Trial windows are about 5-13 s (30 s on d1). Mastery has `setN.` ids: 2 sets on d2-d7, **5 sets on d8 (3075 ids, 22 s)","-  and d9 (3475 ids, 30 s)**, 2 sets again on d10 (1506 ids, 32 s), d11 (1622 ids, 11 s), d12 (1710 ids, 30 s), d13 (1826 ids, 80 s) and d14 (1942 ids, 30 s); **5 sets again on d15 (5130 ids, untimed regular pool)**. The artifact was `evidence-0N.zip`, or (d6) `delivery N: evidence.zip`, or (d7-d9) ONE download","-  `evidence-01.zip` that holds every `evidence-0N.zip`. Same-named deliveries: pair them by sha256. Timed question texts","-  carry `[assigned-artifact-sha256:<hex>]` per member -- usable to verify the bytes you got.","+  (d10, 753) -> +TypeScript (d11, 811) -> +AutoIt (d12, 855) -> +AppleScript (d13, 913) -> +MSBuild `.proj` (d14, 971) -> +Perl","+  + perl_cgi host (d15, 1026) -> +Ruby `.rb` + ruby_rack host (d16, 1095; 123 members). Most days also add 2 Bash advanced","+  fixtures (not d12, d15). Since D8 the TITLE/PROMPT is a pun or narrative; the new language shows up only in the member list","+  (D16 \"Same Same, But Different\" = \"obfuscation equivalence\", and the new files were Ruby). Diff the contract ids against yesterday's.","+- From day 2 on, every fixture hides a **self-describing plan**: `v=N|steps=a,b|adapter=..|stage_count=..|campaign_id=..|<indicators>`.","+  It sits behind a codec, usually named in a `Codec_<id>` / `CODEC_<id>` / `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` const of the form `rep|transform|key`.","+  Most exact_text answers are plan values copied verbatim. From D8 there is also a **`v=3` plan**: it carries `role=` and `attack=`","+  itself, and sits behind a `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-` comment.","+- The hard part is **naming CODE SHAPE**: control-flow, expansion, and function/invocation/property styles. These are GM synthetic","+  labels that are not in the plan. Role and scenario are enums, so read `accepted_values`.","+- Files are named by behaviour (host-context, memory-stage, embedded-write, remote-write, local-dispatch, staged-handoff/-chain,","+  outbound-transfer, impact-plan, relay-handoff, schedule-descriptor). Answer-id = `<lang>-<role>-<field>`; the artifact path picks","+  the file. Don't trust the file name over the plan `steps`.","+- Narrative prompts (D8 \"doesn't match its siblings\", D15 \"a store that was never there\", D16 \"prove which ones are truly","+  equivalent, expose the variant that quietly changed the plot\") have NEVER been asked as a question. Answer the contract ids only.","+- Time Trial windows ~5-17 s. Mastery has `setN.` ids: 2 sets d2-d7 and d10-d14, **5 sets d8, d9, d15 (5130 ids) and d16 (5475","+  ids)**. The artifact was `evidence-0N.zip`, `delivery N: evidence.zip` (d6), or one `evidence-01.zip` holding every","+  `evidence-0N.zip` (d7-d9). Same-named deliveries: pair by sha256. Timed questions carry `[assigned-artifact-sha256:<hex>]`.","+  From D15 the timed contracts are the untimed regular pool (`run_for_time:false`, `variant_fresh:true`, no deadline)."," "," ## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants of the SAME day -- parse every value listed)","-Each miss below cost one failed timed attempt + a ~45-90 s generalize cycle (D6 replay: 4 cycles; D7: 1 cycle; D8-D14: 0;","-D15: 1 TT localize + 1 Mastery cycle with 2 generalize workers, ~5 min, all from the GM-LABEL-REGIME axis below).","-- **GM label regime per pool (D15, NEW; batch `expansion`)** -- SAME bytes, SAME question text, DIFFERENT label. Single solve","-  (no `run_for_time` key) and every older D3-D14 timed case label the whole handoff: `echo(!var!)` => `delayed` unless a FOR/h-pool","-  rule fires. The D15 untimed regular pool (contract `run_for_time:false`, `variant_fresh:true`; TT 0df5072d, Mastery 7fbfc526)","-  labels the JOIN STATEMENT ALONE (54 GM labels, 0 conflicts): `!a!!b!` join = delayed; `for %%G in (..) do call set` = for_indirect","-  for ANY pool (incl. `%%h%%G%%` with an `if defined` reset -- old regime said call_double); bare `call set \"x=%%h0%%..\"` (h pool)","-  = call_double; bare `call set` over item/v_a/FrAg pools = percent; plain `set \"x=%a%%b%\"` = percent. The diff is in the","-  contract's metadata, not the bytes -- two generalize workers burned time diffing byte-identical files. Parse rule: branch","-  the label table on `contract.get(\"run_for_time\") is False`; otherwise keep the old regime. Expect other synthetic-label fields","-  (control/style) to be able to flip the same way: when byte-identical constructs get different GM labels across cases,","-  diff the CONTRACT keys (run_for_time, hall_of_fame_eligible, variant_fresh) first.","-- **Codec per file** -- rep x transform x key re-rolls per variant; never bind a role to the sample's codec. **NEW rep","-  NAMES appear only on variants** (D7 TT: `unicode_escapes` `\\u00XX..`, `json_numbers` `[232,241,..]`,","-  `reversed_base64`, Bash `xor_hex|cd`). Decode by the material's SHAPE (escapes / int array / hex / base64, each also","-  reversed) x the named transform, and accept only output starting `v=`; the name only orders the tries.","-  D9-D15: no rep/transform beyond lib.codec's D3-D8 vocabulary (0 decode failures).","-- **Codec spec arity** -- 3 fields `rep|transform|key`, 2 fields `rep|` (empty transform = identity; D7-D9 bash advanced","-  fixtures), or the transform folded into the rep with the key second (`xor_hex|cd`, D8 `xor_hex|11`, D9 `xor_hex|95/6f/c0`).","-  Split on `|`, never index blindly. lib.codec (`_spec`) normalises both short forms.","-- **Plan carrier tag (v=3, D8-D9)** -- `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-<data>`, plus the same data in `descriptor_<id> = \"..\"`.","-  Values: `B64` (base64), `HEX` (plain hex), `HB64` (hex of base64 text = 2 layers), `FRAG` (hex split by `.` every 24 chars).","-  Across every delivery D8-D15 the tag stayed fixed per file; only the values re-rolled. Parse rule: ignore the tag","-  name. Peel by shape and recurse (max 3 layers): if the text is only hex digits plus `.:,-_ |\\x%` separators, strip the","-  separators and unhex; otherwise base64 (also reversed). Accept only a result starting `v=`. The tag = `obfuscation_profile`.","-  `lib.codec.find_codecs(src)` returns the v=3 plan (tag -> rep: B64 base64_literal, HEX/FRAG hex_compact, HB64 hex_base64).","-- **Plan carrier host syntax (v=3)** -- the marker sits in whatever comment the host uses: `//` (PHP, JS, HTA, WSF, SCT CDATA,","-  MOF, TS), `--` (Lua D9, AppleScript D13), `;` (AutoIt, D12), `<!-- -->` (MSBuild XML, D14), `#` (Perl, D15), and the descriptor as `$descriptor_<id>`, `var descriptor_<id>`, `local","-  descriptor_<id>`, `Global Const $descriptor_<id> = \"..\"` (AutoIt), `property descriptor_<id> : \"..\"` (AppleScript), an XML property element `<PropertyGroup><HuntressDescriptor>..</HuntressDescriptor>`","-  (MSBuild, D14 -- no `descriptor_` name at all), `my $descriptor_<id> = \"..\";` (Perl, D15). Parse rule: regex","-  `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V\\d+\\s*:\\s*(\\w*)-?\\s*([^\\s\"'<>\\]]+)` over the raw bytes, independent of comment syntax and extension.","-- **Numeric literal radix** -- the same array/constant may be decimal `23,7`, hex `0x17,0x07`, or a separator-joined","-  string decoded with `parseInt(x, R)` / `int(x, R)`: READ THE RADIX FROM THE CODE, never guess it from the digits","-  (D6: JScript material array hex on TT; Mastery dash-joined DECIMALS with `parseInt(..,10)`). Applies to keys too.","-- **Base64 alphabet** -- standard and urlsafe (`-` `_`) both occur; strip/whitelist accordingly and pad (D6 Python TT).","-- **Reversal level** -- `reversed_hex/_decimal/_integer_list` reverse the loaded LIST; `reversed_base64` reverses the","-  TEXT before decoding (`==Adu..`). Try both orders.","-- **Carrier of the same language** -- plain source vs a frozen executable (D6: Python plan inside a cx_Freeze build on","-  a TT variant). Locate the material by its markers (`MATERIAL_`/`CODEC_`/`v=`/`HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_`), not by file type.","-- **Material layout** -- one literal, split chunks, `+=` concatenation, adjacent quoted strings, `.`-separated FRAG","-  fragments; join before decoding.","+Each miss cost one failed timed attempt + a ~45-90 s generalize cycle (D6: 4 cycles; D7: 1; D8-D14: 0; D15: TT localize + 1","+Mastery cycle; D16: 0 answer misses -- the Mastery failures were runner timeouts, no bytes reached a verdict).","+- **GM label regime (batch `expansion`; D15 pool-keyed, D16 DATE-keyed)** -- SAME bytes, SAME question text, DIFFERENT label.","+  Old regime (every D3-D14 case + the D15 single): the whole handoff is labelled, `echo(!var!)` => `delayed` unless a FOR/h-pool","+  rule fires. Statement regime (D15 TT/Mastery `run_for_time:false`; **D16 single with NO run_for_time key**; D16 TT a719c002):","+  label the JOIN STATEMENT alone -- `!a!!b!` join = delayed; `for %%G in (..) do call set` = for_indirect for ANY pool (incl. an h","+  pool); bare `call set \"x=%%h0%%..\"` (h pool) = call_double; bare `call set` over item/v_a/FrAg pools = percent; plain","+  `set \"x=%a%%b%\"` = percent. D16 single GM labels: benign for_indirect, stager/dropper delayed, downloader call_double,","+  uploader/launcher/impact/chain/relay percent. The D15 rule \"branch on run_for_time\" was keyed on the wrong thing and cost 5","+  rejected probes on the D16 single. Parse rule: **statement regime is the default** (`run_for_time is False` OR","+  `started_at >= 2026-10-16`); the old regime only for older replayed cases. When byte-identical constructs get different GM","+  labels across cases, tabulate (construct, label) against EVERY contract key (started_at, run_for_time, variant_fresh,","+  hall_of_fame_eligible) at once instead of diffing bytes. Expect other synthetic labels (control/style) to flip the same way.","+- **Codec per file** -- rep x transform x key re-rolls per variant; never bind a role to the sample's codec. **NEW rep NAMES","+  appear only on variants** (D7 TT: `unicode_escapes`, `json_numbers`, `reversed_base64`, Bash `xor_hex|cd`). Decode by the","+  material's SHAPE (escapes / int array / hex / base64, each also reversed) x the named transform; accept only output starting","+  `v=`; the name only orders the tries. D9-D16: nothing beyond lib.codec's vocabulary (0 decode failures).","+- **Codec spec arity** -- `rep|transform|key`, `rep|` (empty transform = identity; Bash advanced D7-D16), or transform folded","+  into the rep with the key second (`xor_hex|cd`, D16 `xor_hex|ec`). Split on `|`, never index blindly (lib.codec `_spec`).","+- **Plan carrier tag (v=3, D8-D16)** -- `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-<data>` + the same data in a descriptor literal. Tags `B64`,","+  `HEX`, `HB64` (hex of base64), `FRAG` (hex split by `.` every 24 chars); stayed fixed per file in every delivery D8-D16, only","+  values re-rolled. Parse rule: ignore the tag name; peel by shape, recurse (max 3-4 layers); accept only `v=`. Tag =","+  `obfuscation_profile` (B64 base64, HEX plain_hex, HB64 hex_base64, FRAG fragmented_hex). `lib.codec.find_codecs(src)` returns it.","+- **Plan carrier host syntax (v=3)** -- marker in whatever comment the host uses: `//` (PHP, JS, HTA, WSF, SCT, MOF, TS), `--`","+  (Lua, AppleScript), `;` (AutoIt), `<!-- -->` (MSBuild), `#` (Perl D15, Ruby D16). Descriptor forms: `$descriptor_<id>`,","+  `var/local descriptor_<id>`, `Global Const $descriptor_<id>`, `property descriptor_<id> :`, `<HuntressDescriptor>` element","+  (MSBuild, no name), `my $descriptor_<id> = \"..\";` (Perl), **`DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX> = \"..\"` uppercase Ruby constant (D16)**. Parse rule:","+  regex `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V\\d+\\s*:\\s*(\\w*)-?\\s*([^\\s\"'<>\\]]+)` over raw bytes, independent of comment syntax, case and extension.","+- **Numeric literal radix** -- decimal `23,7`, hex `0x17`, or a joined string read with `parseInt(x, R)` / `int(x, R)`: READ THE","+  RADIX FROM THE CODE (D6 JScript TT hex; Mastery dash-joined DECIMALS). Applies to keys too.","+- **Base64 alphabet** -- standard and urlsafe (`-` `_`) both occur; whitelist and pad (D6 Python TT).","+- **Reversal level** -- `reversed_hex/_decimal/_integer_list` reverse the LIST; `reversed_base64` reverses the TEXT. Try both.","+- **Carrier of the same language** -- plain source vs a frozen executable (D6 TT: Python plan in a cx_Freeze build). Locate","+  material by markers (`MATERIAL_`/`CODEC_`/`v=`/`HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_`), not by file type.","+- **Material layout** -- one literal, split chunks, `+=`, adjacent quoted strings, `.`-separated FRAG; join before decoding."," - **Adapter values** re-roll within a role (Node stager http_then_module/https_then_vm/fetch_then_function; launcher","   execfile_node/fork_module/spawn_file; persistence systemd_descriptor/npm_lifecycle_descriptor) -- always plan-verbatim.","-- **No-new-axis days** (bytes): D8-D14 and D15 (TT 0df5072d, Mastery 7fbfc526; the 4 `.pl` + perl_cgi host kept tags/steps/","-  next_language in all 6 deliveries). Structure, tags, role/attack/steps/profiles identical to the single; only values","-  re-rolled. D8-D14 all CORRECT first try; D15's only misses came from the label-regime axis above.","+- **Transport/runner, not variant** -- D7 TT saved `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` as the zip; D8 TT start 503","+  `training_rotation_invalid`; D16 Mastery (5 sets, 5475 ids, 3.2-3.7 MB status bodies at 5-8 s each) hit the 60 s local","+  `hb_timed` cap on all 5 attempts (`exec_error`, nothing submitted). None of these is a solver change; never harvest them as cases."," "," ## Recognition cues -> first move"," | You see | First move |"," |---|---|","-| `evidence.zip`, \"method=AES Encrypted\" | Already extracted by triage (`work/extracted/`, password `infected`) and every plan decoded in triage.md -- start from that, BUT diff the extracted member list against the contract's `artifact` names. **Triage silently skips each day's new extension**: D7 `.mjs`, D8 `.php` (HB64 peeled 1 layer only), D9 `.lua` (5 files, no decode lines). In solve.py open members with `lib.common.read_member` (Python zipfile cannot read AES). Mastery may be a zip inside a zip; walk it once. |","-| Prior-day languages in the contract | Cumulative: derive every family from TODAY's bytes with the shared codec method below. Spend thinking on the new language. If yesterday's solver routes by plan MARKER (not extension) it may already cover today (D9: unchanged D8 solver, 695/695). |","-| `.ps1` with `$encodedMaterial = [Convert]::FromBase64String('..')` + `$reconstruct` + `$nativeTypes` | `base64 -d` -> JSON descriptor (short keys a/b/c..): url/wallet/mutex/UA/file/ext/note. Match indicators by SHAPE, not key. `$nativeTypes` gives the scenario: Process/Registry+wallet=resource, ZipFile/HttpWebRequest=collection, Aes/DirectoryInfo=impact. |","-| `.js` WSH, `decode_*`/`recover_*`/`inspect_*`, XOR key arrays, `\"52:90:..\"` strings | Run each file in an empty `node` `vm` context (no require/ActiveXObject), `eval` swapped for a capture. Call the top-level functions and keep the first object that has `steps`. Read the styles off the `inspect_*` body. |","-| Timed contract with `run_for_time: false` / `variant_fresh: true` | Untimed regular pool (D15): batch `expansion` uses the statement-only label table (Variant axes). Check this key before trusting labels harvested from the single or from older timed cases. |","-| `.bat/.cmd` with `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` / `HUNTRESS-MATERIAL:`, `set \"itemN=v=1|steps=..`, `:HUNTRESS_INSPECT` | Plan is in plain `set` fragments. Emulate cmd expansion in Python (`%v%`, `!v!`, `call set %%..%%`, `for %%G in (..)`). The MATERIAL line is a 2nd encoded copy to cross-check. Never run cmd. |","-| `.vbs` with `Const Material_<id>`, `Const Codec_<id> = \"rep|transform|key\"`, `Load_/Decode_/Recover_<id>` | Decode in Python from the Codec const, cross-check against the Load/Decode code (no cscript). rep/transform answers = Codec fields 1/2 verbatim. Control = the construct wrapping the `Decode_` call inside `Recover_`. |","-| `.py` `*-recovered.py` with `MATERIAL_<id>`, `CODEC_<id>`, `load_/decode_/surface_/plan_<id>` | Already-recovered source (no decompile on d5). Decode from CODEC or run `decode_(load_(MATERIAL))` under an AST whitelist. Plan v=2 carries syntax/obfuscation/carrier/windows_chain verbatim. |","-| `.sh` `readonly Material_<id>='..'` + `readonly Codec_<id>='rep|transform|key'` | Decode from the Codec const (key hex; multi-byte key = COMMA list). Re-join split/`+=`/adjacent-quoted chunks. Never run bash. |","-| `.sh` with `Feature_<id>()` (`${!pointer}`, `local -a parts=('cu' 'rl')`, `local -A`, `${arr[@]:1:2}`, `trap 'return 0' RETURN`, a self-calling `walk_fixture`), plan `v=1|feature=..|primitive=..` | Role `advanced_syntax` (closed enum value). feature/primitive/campaign/stage_count/steps are plan-verbatim; attack = T1059.004. The `Feature_` body is the feature; never name it from the code, copy the plan. |","-| `.mjs` ESM: `const Material_<id> = \"..\"; const Codec_<id> = \"rep|transform|key\"`, async `load_/decode_/recover_/inspect_/plan_<id>`, `process.env.HUNTRESS_INSPECT_ONLY` | Static decode with `lib.codec.find_codecs` + shape fallback (reps hex_buffer, hex_array, escaped_octets `\\\\xNN`, decimal_array, unicode_escapes, json_numbers). Don't run it (top-level await, Buffer/vm). Plan fields verbatim; role from `steps`. |","-| `// HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG>-..` or `-- HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:..` + `descriptor_<id> = \"..\"` (`.php`; `.lua` `local descriptor_..` + `build_plan_<id>`, OpenResty `inert_handler_<id>` returning `{status=200,..}`; `.js` that is really HTA `<hta:application>`, WSF `<job><script language=\"JScript\">` or SCT `<?xml?><scriptlet><registration progid=..>` CDATA; `.vbs` that is a WSF job; `.au3` AutoIt `; HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:` + `Global Const $descriptor_..`; `.proj` MSBuild `<!-- HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:..-->` + `<HuntressDescriptor>`; `.pl` Perl `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:` + `use strict;` + `my $descriptor_..`) | **Route by the marker, before the extension** (the extension lies). Peel the descriptor by shape to `v=3|language=..|role=..|verdict=..|attack=..|adapter=..|host_profile=..|obfuscation_profile=..|stage_profile=..|next_language=..|stage_count=..|steps=..|campaign_id=..|url=..|file_path=..`. EVERY answer, including role and attack, is plan-verbatim. Python `-I` + base64/bytes.fromhex is enough. |","-| Real `.pyc` / PyInstaller / pyarmor (not seen yet) | `lib.pyc.recover_python(path)` (pyinstxtractor-ng + decompyle3, `dis` fallback). See skills/script-analysis. |","-| Any `Codec_` key like `ba` / `0a` | A hex byte, not text. Transforms are named for the ENCODE side: `subtract_modulo_256` decodes by ADDING, `add_modulo_256` by SUBTRACTING. `rolling_xor` = c ^ previous CIPHER byte, seeded with the key. |","+| `evidence.zip`, \"method=AES Encrypted\" | Triage already extracted it (`work/extracted/`) and decoded every plan. Diff the member list / contract ids against yesterday's to find the new language (D16: 4 `polyglot-ruby-*.rb` + `host-ruby-rack-ruby.rb` + 2 `.sh`). Triage used to skip new extensions (D7 `.mjs`, D8 `.php`, D9 `.lua`); D15-D16 it decoded them. Open members with `lib.common.read_member` (zipfile can't read AES). |","+| Prior-day languages in the contract | Cumulative: rerun the carried marker-routed solver FIRST (D9-D16: it covered each new v=3 language unchanged). Spend thinking on the new language and on synthetic-label regimes. |","+| `.ps1` `$encodedMaterial = [Convert]::FromBase64String('..')` + `$nativeTypes` | `base64 -d` -> JSON descriptor: url/wallet/mutex/UA/file/ext/note by SHAPE. `$nativeTypes` gives the scenario: Process/Registry+wallet=resource, ZipFile/HttpWebRequest=collection, Aes/DirectoryInfo=impact. |","+| `.js` WSH, `decode_*`/`recover_*`/`inspect_*`, XOR key arrays, `\"52:90:..\"` | Run each file in an empty `node` `vm` (no require/ActiveXObject, `eval` -> capture); keep the first object with `steps`. Styles come off the `inspect_*` body. |","+| `.bat/.cmd` `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` / `HUNTRESS-MATERIAL:`, `set \"itemN=..`, `:HUNTRESS_INSPECT` | Plan is in `set` fragments. Emulate cmd expansion in Python. MATERIAL = second encoded copy to cross-check. Expansion label: statement regime by default (Variant axes). Never run cmd. |","+| `.vbs` `Const Material_<id>`, `Const Codec_<id> = \"rep|transform|key\"` | Decode from the Codec const; rep/transform answers = Codec fields 1/2 verbatim. Control = construct wrapping `Decode_` inside `Recover_`. |","+| `.py` `*-recovered.py` with `MATERIAL_<id>`, `CODEC_<id>` | Decode from CODEC (or AST-whitelisted `decode_(load_(..))`). Plan v=2 carries syntax/obfuscation/carrier/windows_chain verbatim. |","+| `.sh` `readonly Material_<id>` + `readonly Codec_<id>` (+ `Feature_<id>()`) | Decode from the Codec const (multi-byte key = COMMA list). `Feature_` fixtures: role `advanced_syntax`, feature/primitive/campaign/stage_count/steps plan-verbatim, attack T1059.004. Never run bash. |","+| `.mjs` ESM `const Material_<id>`, async `load_/decode_/recover_/inspect_/plan_<id>` | Static decode (`lib.codec.find_codecs` + shape fallback). Don't run it. Plan fields verbatim; role from `steps`. |","+| `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG>-..` in any comment + a descriptor literal (`.php .lua .js(HTA/WSF/SCT) .vbs(WSF) .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb`) | **Route by the marker before the extension.** Peel to `v=3|language=..|role=..|attack=..|adapter=..|host_profile=..|obfuscation_profile=..|stage_profile=..|next_language=..|stage_count=..|steps=..|campaign_id=..|url=..|file_path=..`. EVERY answer incl. role/attack is plan-verbatim. |","+| Timed contract `run_for_time:false`, or any contract started on/after 2026-10-16 | Batch `expansion` = statement-only table. Check the contract keys before trusting labels harvested from older cases. |","+| Real `.pyc` / PyInstaller / pyarmor (not seen yet) | `lib.pyc.recover_python(path)` (pyinstxtractor-ng + decompyle3, `dis` fallback). |","+| `Codec_` key like `ba` / `0a` / `ec` | A hex byte. Transforms are ENCODE-side names: `subtract_modulo_256` decodes by ADDING; `rolling_xor` = c ^ previous CIPHER byte, seeded with the key. |"," ","-## Codec table (`Codec_<id>='<rep>|<transform>|<key>'`, batch `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:<rep>|<transform>`; seen D3-D9)","-**Already done for you:** triage.md's \"Decoded payloads\" runs `lib.codec` on every declared codec (and a node vm","-sandbox on JScript). In solve.py call `lib.codec.find_codecs(text)` / `lib.codec.decode(material, rep, transform, key)`","-(pure Python, Homebase-safe, unknown names -> None). A line `NOT decoded by lib.codec` = new rep/transform/arity: decode","-it by material shape yourself and list it under `## Proposed lib additions` in NOTES.md. D9 added nothing new.","-- Reps (how the bytes are WRITTEN): base64_literal/_chunks, urlsafe_base64, reversed_base64 (D7); hex_pairs/_compact/","-  _colon/_dash/_escape (`\\x`)/_literal (`0x`)/_buffer/_array (`[\"69\",\"22\"]`), percent_hex (`%xx`), escaped_octets","-  (`\\\\xNN`), unicode_escapes (`\\\\u00NN`); decimal_bytes/_comma/_dash/_pipe/_dot/_colon/_space/_csv/_array, json_numbers,","-  integer_list/_tuple, octal_space; reversed_text/_hex/_decimal/_integer_list; plain_fragments/split_fragments;","-  v=3 hex_base64 (D8).","-- Transforms (ENCODE-side names; key hex, multi-byte = COMMA list): identity (also EMPTY field), reverse/reverse_bytes,","-  single_byte_xor, repeating_key_xor, reverse_then_xor, rolling_xor (2 flavours), add_modulo_256 (decode SUBTRACTS),","-  subtract_modulo_256 (decode ADDS); batch carries the parameter in the name: xor_5a, add_7 (decimal), rotate_left","-  (undo = rotate right), reverse_xor; bash `xor_hex|<key>` = hex then XOR key (D7-D9).","-- Check: the decoded plaintext starts `v=` (or `{` JSON). If not, the codec reading is wrong.","+## Codec table (`Codec_<id>='<rep>|<transform>|<key>'`, batch `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:<rep>|<transform>`; seen D3-D16)","+**Already done for you:** triage.md's \"Decoded payloads\" runs `lib.codec` on every declared codec (and a node vm sandbox on","+JScript). In solve.py: `lib.codec.find_codecs(text)` / `lib.codec.decode(material, rep, transform, key)` (pure Python,","+unknown names -> None). `NOT decoded by lib.codec` = new rep/transform/arity: decode by shape, note it under `## Proposed lib additions`.","+- Reps: base64_literal/_chunks, urlsafe_base64, reversed_base64; hex_pairs/_compact/_colon/_dash/_escape (`\\x`)/_literal (`0x`)/","+  _buffer/_array, percent_hex, escaped_octets, unicode_escapes; decimal_bytes/_comma/_dash/_pipe/_dot/_colon/_space/_csv/_array,","+  json_numbers, integer_list/_tuple, octal_space; reversed_text/_hex/_decimal/_integer_list; plain/split_fragments; v=3 hex_base64.","+- Transforms (key hex, multi-byte = COMMA list): identity (also EMPTY), reverse/reverse_bytes, single_byte_xor, repeating_key_xor,","+  reverse_then_xor, rolling_xor (2 flavours), add_modulo_256 (decode SUBTRACTS), subtract_modulo_256 (decode ADDS); batch names","+  carry the parameter: xor_5a, add_7 (decimal), rotate_left, reverse_xor; bash `xor_hex|<key>` = unhex then XOR.","+- Check: plaintext starts `v=` (or `{` JSON). If not, the codec reading is wrong."," "," ## Day by day","-**D1-D7 (PS 15 -> +JScript -> +Batch -> +VBScript -> +Python -> +Bash -> +Node, 469 ids)**: D1 collection ATT&CK cost 5","-wrong before `T1555.003` (map the SPECIFIC artifact); D2 handoff = `staged_chain`, 7 wrong ATT&CK guesses; **D3 ~1 h 45 min,","-~127 rejected probes** on batch expansion/control labels -> NAMING LAWS; D4 VBS control probed one field at a time (4 wrong);","-D5-D6 0 wrong, ~4 min (plan v=2; stage_count = plan field, not len(steps)); D7 469/469 in ~100 s, TT missed 15 ids on new reps","-and one attempt saved `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` as the zip -> **diagnose EVERY failed attempt, not only the latest.**","-**D8-D14 (+PHP polyglot & 4 host formats, +Lua/SCT/OpenResty, +WMI MOF, +TypeScript, +AutoIt, +AppleScript, +MSBuild `.proj`;","-+2 Bash advanced most days; 615 -> 971 ids)**: D8 introduced the v=3 plan (`HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-` + descriptor, byte-identical;","-role/attack/adapter/profiles stated -- **copy, don't derive**); 6 ids lost once to hyphenated family names (longest-known-suffix","-field parse). Since then each new language = 4 polyglots (role benign_utility/downloader/launcher/staged_chain, attack","-none/T1105/T1059/T1059, adapter local_parser/http_client/process_builder/operation_graph, obfuscation plain_hex/base64/hex_base64/","-fragmented_hex, campaign `<LANG>-<8hex>`, url `https://<lang>-<10hex>.example.invalid/stage`, file_path","-`/tmp/huntress-<lang>/.<16hex>.stage`). D14 family has an UNDERSCORE (`polyglot-msbuild_xml-..`, campaign `MSBUILD_XML-..`);","-its prompt's MSBuild ATT&CK (T1127.001) was NOT the answer, the plan said T1059. Narrative prompts (impossible family tree,","-reboot-surviving subscription, archive delivery chain, trusted toolchain) were never asked. Marker-routed solver unchanged, 0","-wrong, all modes first try (single T+11 s on D14; TT 3-7 s, mostly GM latency).","-**D15 Crumb Trail (+4 Perl `.pl` polyglot + 1 Perl host; 1026 ids, 116 members)**: prompt \"credential-access-shaped code","-rummaging through the browser's cupboards ... find the reference that points at a store that was never there\" -- flavour only;","-no credential-store/outlier question was asked (the PS collection fixture stayed T1555.003).","-- New: `polyglot-perl-{benign-utility,downloader,launcher,staged-chain}.pl` and `host-perl-cgi-perl.pl` = `#!/usr/bin/env perl` +","-  `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<HEX|B64|HB64|FRAG>-..` + `use strict; use warnings; my $descriptor_<id> = \"..\";` (same data).","-  Plan v=3 `language=perl`, campaign `PERL-<8hex>`, url `https://perl-<10hex>.example.invalid/stage`, file_path","-  `/tmp/huntress-perl/.<16hex>.stage`, host_profile `standalone` / `perl_cgi`. Every answer plan-verbatim (host perl_cgi =","-  staged_chain/T1059/operation_graph; downloader T1105; benign `none`). Triage decoded the `.pl` plans this time.","-- Single: carried-over marker-routed solver, harness race probe 1026/1026 CORRECT at T+17 s, 0 wrong.","-- TT 0df5072d (untimed regular pool): 8 batch-expansion ids `delayed` -> GM `percent`; localize fixed them, CORRECT at 39 s.","-  Mastery 7fbfc526 (5 sets, 5130 ids): ~25 expansion ids wrong in all 5 sets; 2 generalize workers found the","-  `run_for_time:false` statement-only regime (Variant axes); re-run left 1 miss (`set5.batch-chain-expansion`, h-pool FOR =","-  for_indirect, not call_double) fixed by localize; CORRECT ~5.5 min after start. Everything else first try.","+**D1-D7 (PS -> +JScript -> +Batch -> +VBScript -> +Python -> +Bash -> +Node, 469 ids)**: D1 collection ATT&CK cost 5 wrong before","+`T1555.003`; D2 handoff = `staged_chain`, 7 wrong ATT&CK guesses; **D3 ~1 h 45 min, ~127 rejected probes** on batch","+expansion/control labels -> NAMING LAWS; D4 VBS control probed one field at a time (4 wrong); D5-D6 0 wrong (~4 min; stage_count =","+plan field); D7 469/469 in ~100 s, TT missed 15 ids on new reps + one `rate_limited` body saved as the zip.","+**D8-D15 (+PHP polyglot & hosts, Lua/SCT/OpenResty, MOF, TS, AutoIt, AppleScript, MSBuild, Perl; 615 -> 1026 ids)**: D8 introduced","+v=3 (copy role/attack/adapter/profiles, don't derive); 6 ids lost once to hyphenated family names. Each new language = 4 polyglots","+(benign_utility/downloader/launcher/staged_chain; attack none/T1105/T1059/T1059; adapter local_parser/http_client/process_builder/","+operation_graph; campaign `<LANG>-<8hex>`, url `https://<lang>-<10hex>.example.invalid/stage`, file_path","+`/tmp/huntress-<lang>/.<16hex>.stage`) + sometimes one `host-<profile>-<lang>` file. D14 family had an underscore (`msbuild_xml`)","+and its prompt's ATT&CK (T1127.001) was NOT the answer (plan said T1059). D8-D14 all modes first try. D15: single 1026/1026 at","+T+17 s; TT and Mastery (5 sets) missed ~25 batch-expansion ids -> the label-regime axis; CORRECT ~5.5 min after start.","+**D16 Same Same, But Different (`obfuscation-equivalence`; +4 Ruby `.rb` polyglot + `host-ruby-rack-ruby.rb` + Bash advanced","+`ansi-c-quoting.sh`, `regex-conditional.sh`; 1095 ids, 123 members)**:","+- Prompt: \"several obfuscation families scrambled the same logic ... prove which are truly equivalent, expose the variant that","+  quietly changed the plot\". Flavour only: no equivalence/outlier question; every id was the usual per-file family.","+- Ruby fixture: `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..` + `DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX> = \"..\"` (uppercase constant). Plan v=3 `language=ruby`;","+  host_profile `standalone` / `ruby_rack` (host = staged_chain/T1059/operation_graph). `steps` answers are `>`-joined","+  (ordered_tokens), e.g. `profile_host>decode_configuration>dispatch_language`; stage_count is the plan field (benign = 2).","+  next_language values seen: powershell, jscript, batch, vbscript. All plan-verbatim; the carried solver decoded them unchanged.","+- Bash advanced (plan-verbatim): `ansi_c_quoting|ansi_c_escape_string` (`$'node\\nbash\\tfixture'`), `regex_conditional|","+  bash_regex_match` (`[[ $v =~ ^node-[0-9]+$ ]]`); codecs `hex_compact|` and `xor_hex|ec`.","+- Single: worker decided \"carried solver covers Ruby\" at T+33 s; the bisecting submit then hit 5 `incorrect` probes on","+  batch-{uploader,launcher,impact,chain,relay}-expansion (`delayed` -> GM `percent`): the single has NO run_for_time key yet used","+  the statement regime. Duel worker switched the regime on `started_at >= 2026-10-16`; CORRECT at T+4 min 23 s.","+- TT a719c002 (`run_for_time:false`): CORRECT first try, 16.7 s (start 6.3, download 2.1, solve 1.4, submit 6.9).","+- Mastery (5 sets, 5475 ids): 5/5 attempts `exec_error` \"local hb_timed timed out\" (60 s runner cap) -- the start/download/","+  submit of a 5475-id bundle does not fit the cap; no answers reached the GM, so no variant axis could be observed."," "," ## GM answer conventions learned","-- **Check `answer_format.kind` first.** `enum` gives the list (scenario, role). `mitre_attack_id` takes `T####[.###]` or literal `none` (benign_utility). `integer`/`ordered_tokens` (d6+). `exact_text` = plan value or synthetic label.","-- **Plan-verbatim fields** (copy exactly):","-  - adapter: COM ProgIDs `MSXML2.ServerXMLHTTP.6.0`, LOLBins `CertReq.exe`, batch `call`/`set`/`for`, Node","-    `console_report`/`typed_array_to_file`/`stream_pipeline`, v=3 local_parser/runtime_loader/file_writer/http_client/","-    process_builder/schedule_builder/operation_graph.","-  - indicators: campaign_id, host_id, url, file_path, upload_url, next_stage, extension, note_name, handoff_id, cron_path,","-    schedule_path, service_name. Indicator questions read \"exact X indicator\", where X is the plan key.","-  - per-language labels: batch `graph` (D9 confirmed linear/single/diamond/fan_out/fallback_retry/cross_language/","-    same_language), Python syntax/obfuscation/carrier/windows_chain, Bash feature/primitive, v=3 host_profile/","-    obfuscation_profile/stage_profile/next_language.","-  - v=3 host_profile seen: standalone, wsf_jscript, wsf_mixed, hta_jscript, php_webshell (D8), sct_scriptlet, lua_openresty","-    (D9), perl_cgi (D15). obfuscation: base64/plain_hex/hex_base64/fragmented_hex. stage_profile: single_descriptor/","-    two_stage_download_execute/three_stage_decode_write_launch/cross_language_handoff.","-  - Bash advanced feature|primitive (always plan-verbatim; 14 seen D7-D14), e.g. indirect_expansion|parameter_indirection,","-    associative_arrays|declare_associative, heredoc_reconstruction|quoted_heredoc, getopts_state|option_parser_state (D14),","-    brace_expansion|cartesian_brace_expansion (D14). Family = `bash-advanced-<file-stem>` (D7 short forms: `indirect`, `tokens`).","-  - **v=3 role and attack too.** GM accepted the plan's PARENT technique ids: `T1059` (launcher, staged_chain -- PHP, WSF,","-    HTA, SCT, Lua alike) and `T1053` (persistence_descriptor), NOT the host-language sub-technique. The role->ATT&CK table","-    below is for v=1/v=2 plans only. **v=3 role does NOT follow `steps`** (D14 MSBuild: benign_utility had steps","-    `decode_embedded>write_file>dispatch_process`, launcher `decode_configuration>return_configuration`) -- copy role= and steps=","-    independently; never \"fix\" one from the other.","-- **Role from `steps`** (v=1/v=2 plans; v=3 states `role=`):","-","-  | steps | role |","-  |---|---|","-  | decode_configuration,return_configuration | benign_utility |","-  | acquire_remote + dispatch_memory/dispatch_pipe | stager |","-  | acquire_remote,write_file | downloader |","-  | decode_embedded,write_file | dropper |","-  | locate_local,dispatch_process | launcher |","-  | read_file/upload,transmit_remote | uploader |","-  | transform + recovery_note | impact |","-  | build_schedule,register_descriptor (Node d7) | persistence_descriptor |","-  | recognize_syntax,reconstruct_intent + plan `feature=` (Bash d7-d9) | advanced_syntax |","-  | ends in handoff_script (JS/Batch/VBS) or profile_host..dispatch_process | staged_chain |","-  | dispatch_next_stage (Python) | relay |","-","+- **Check `answer_format.kind` first.** `enum` lists values (scenario, role). `mitre_attack_id` takes `T####[.###]` or literal","+  `none` (benign_utility). `integer`/`ordered_tokens` (d6+; steps joined with `>`). `exact_text` = plan value or synthetic label.","+- **Plan-verbatim fields** (copy exactly): adapter (COM ProgIDs `MSXML2.ServerXMLHTTP.6.0`, LOLBins `CertReq.exe`/`curl.exe`/","+  `cipher.exe`, batch `call`/`set`/`for`, Node `console_report`.., v=3 local_parser/runtime_loader/file_writer/http_client/","+  process_builder/schedule_builder/operation_graph); indicators (campaign_id, host_id, url, file_path, upload_url, next_stage,","+  extension, note_name, handoff_id, cron_path, schedule_path, service_name -- question reads \"exact X indicator\", X = plan key);","+  batch `graph` (linear/single/diamond/fan_out/fallback_retry/cross_language/same_language); Python syntax/obfuscation/carrier/","+  windows_chain; Bash feature/primitive (16 seen D7-D16); v=3 host_profile (standalone, wsf_jscript, wsf_mixed, hta_jscript,","+  php_webshell, sct_scriptlet, lua_openresty, perl_cgi, ruby_rack), obfuscation (base64/plain_hex/hex_base64/fragmented_hex),","+  stage_profile (single_descriptor/two_stage_download_execute/three_stage_decode_write_launch/cross_language_handoff), next_language.","+- **v=3 role and attack too.** GM accepted the plan's PARENT ids `T1059` (launcher, staged_chain, every host) and `T1053`","+  (persistence_descriptor). **v=3 role does NOT follow `steps`** (D14 MSBuild, D16 Ruby downloader steps","+  `acquire_remote>dispatch_process`) -- copy role= and steps= independently.","+- **Role from `steps`** (v=1/v=2 only): decode_configuration,return_configuration = benign_utility; acquire_remote +","+  dispatch_memory/pipe = stager; acquire_remote,write_file = downloader; decode_embedded,write_file = dropper; locate_local,","+  dispatch_process = launcher; read_file/upload,transmit_remote = uploader; transform + recovery_note = impact;","+  build_schedule,register_descriptor = persistence_descriptor; recognize_syntax,reconstruct_intent + `feature=` = advanced_syntax;","+  ends in handoff_script or profile_host..dispatch_process = staged_chain; dispatch_next_stage (Python) = relay.","   cron_path/service_name on a staged_chain are indicators only, NOT persistence.","-- **Role -> ATT&CK** (GM-confirmed d2-d9; `lib.scripts.role_attack(role, lang)` has the table):","-  - benign `none`; downloader and stager T1105; dropper T1140; uploader T1041; impact T1486; persistence_descriptor","-    T1053.003 (by role, whatever the adapter); advanced_syntax T1059.004.","-  - launcher/staged_chain/relay follow the HOST LANGUAGE: T1059.003 batch, .004 bash, .005 VBS, .006 python, .007","-    JScript AND Node.js (.001 PS predicted, never asked).","-  - PS scenarios: resource_hijacking T1496, synthetic_collection T1555.003, synthetic_impact T1486.","-  - REJECTED: T1218.010, T1620, T1027.009, T1005, T1560, T1119, T1074(.001); stager T1059.007; dropper T1105.","-- **Batch expansion** (closed set; mined from EVERY GM-verified D3-D6 case, 0 conflicts in 545):","-  - fragments named `h<N>` AND joined with `call set` (bare, or `for %%G in (..) do call set`) = `call_double`","-  - `for %%G in (..) do call set \"cfg=%%cfg%%%%<pool>%%G%%\"` over any OTHER pool (v_a/item/fragment/FrAg) = `for_indirect`","-  - everything else = `delayed`, INCLUDING h-pools joined with `!h0!!h1!..` (the \"h-pool = call_double\" shortcut failed).","-  - Fragment JOINER pitfall: `set \"item9=%item0%%item1%...\"` is the JOIN, not fragment 9 -- skip `set` lines whose","-    value references the other fragments (a wrong Mastery answer on D6).","-  - D13+ question text: \"Classify only the expansion form used by the descriptor reconstruction statement\" with enum","-    percent/delayed/call_double/for_indirect. In the `run_for_time:false` pool the label follows that wording literally","-    (statement-only table under Variant axes); single solve still followed the echo(!var!) rules above.","-  - REJECTED: percent_expansion, immediate, call-double, double_call.","-- **Batch control**: direct (separator lines and `:HUNTRESS_UNUSED` dead labels are NOT control), errorlevel_guard","-  (`ver >nul` + `if errorlevel 1 exit /b 1`), goto_dispatch, call_subroutine, if_guard (`if defined X`). REJECTED:","-  linear, straight_line, sequential, goto, goto_label, double_pipe, pipe, ampersand, call_label, dead_label, errorlevel,","-  opaque_branch, + ~40 \"if defined\" synonyms.","-- **VBS control**: direct, select_case, do_once, while_once, error_guard (`On Error Resume Next`..`Err.Raise`),","-  for_once. REJECTED: do_loop, do_exit, while_wend, while_loop, on_error_resume.","-- **Codec labels**: representation/transform = the codec const's fields 1/2 copied VERBATIM; spellings differ per","-  language (Python `decimal_csv`, batch `decimal_bytes|reverse_xor`): read the const, never translate.","-- **JScript styles** (closed sets in the question text; GM-confirmed D2-D9):","-  - function-style: `function f(` = declaration; `var f = function(` = anonymous_expression; `var f = function f_body(` = named_expression.","-  - invocation-style: how recover/inspect invokes the next top-level function: `f(x)` = direct, `f.call(..)` (also via","-    a local `invoke` helper doing `block.call`) = call, `f.apply(..)` = apply.","-  - property-style: only `o.k` = dot, only `o[\"k\"]` = bracket_literal, both = mixed. triage's `shape:` line counts them.","-- **NAMING LAWS** (proven on if_guard, error_guard, do_once, pe_cli). Compose unknown labels from the SHORT language keyword:","-  - conditional/bail-out = `<keyword>_guard`; run-once loop = `<keyword>_once`; control transfer = `<keyword>_<action>`.","-  - The spelled-out statement (if_defined, on_error_resume, do_exit, while_wend) and descriptive synonyms (flag_guard, defined_guard, opaque_predicate) have ALWAYS been rejected.","+- **Role -> ATT&CK** (v=1/v=2; `lib.scripts.role_attack(role, lang)`): benign `none`; downloader/stager T1105; dropper T1140;","+  uploader T1041; impact T1486; persistence_descriptor T1053.003; advanced_syntax T1059.004; launcher/staged_chain/relay = host","+  language T1059.003 batch / .004 bash / .005 VBS / .006 python / .007 JScript and Node. PS scenarios: resource_hijacking T1496,","+  synthetic_collection T1555.003, synthetic_impact T1486. REJECTED: T1218.010, T1620, T1027.009, T1005, T1560, T1119, T1074(.001);","+  stager T1059.007; dropper T1105.","+- **Batch expansion** (enum percent/delayed/call_double/for_indirect; question \"Classify only the expansion form used by the","+  descriptor reconstruction statement\"): statement regime = Variant axes table (default from D16). Old regime (D3-D14 cases):","+  h-pool + `call set` = call_double; `for .. do call set` over other pools = for_indirect; everything else delayed (incl.","+  `!h0!!h1!`). Fragment JOINER pitfall: `set \"item9=%item0%%item1%..\"` is the JOIN, not fragment 9. REJECTED: percent_expansion,","+  immediate, call-double, double_call.","+- **Batch control**: direct, errorlevel_guard (`ver >nul` + `if errorlevel 1 exit /b 1`), goto_dispatch, call_subroutine,","+  if_guard (`if defined X`); separators and `:HUNTRESS_UNUSED` dead labels are NOT control. ~45 synonyms rejected (D3).","+- **VBS control**: direct, select_case, do_once, while_once, error_guard (`On Error Resume Next`..`Err.Raise`), for_once.","+- **Codec labels**: representation/transform = the codec const's fields 1/2 VERBATIM (per-language spellings differ).","+- **JScript styles**: function-style `function f(` declaration / `var f = function(` anonymous_expression / `var f = function","+  f_body(` named_expression; invocation-style direct / call (`.call`, also via a local invoke helper) / apply; property-style","+  dot / bracket_literal / mixed (triage's `shape:` line counts them).","+- **NAMING LAWS** (proven on if_guard, error_guard, do_once, pe_cli): conditional/bail-out = `<keyword>_guard`; run-once loop =","+  `<keyword>_once`; control transfer = `<keyword>_<action>`. Spelled-out statements (if_defined, on_error_resume, do_exit,","+  while_wend) and descriptive synonyms (flag_guard, opaque_predicate) have ALWAYS been rejected."," "," ## Pitfalls that cost time","-- **Diffing bytes when the regime changed** (D15 Mastery, ~5 min): 25 batch-expansion ids flipped delayed->percent on","-  byte-identical files. Tabulate (join shape, pool, GM label) per contract metadata key at once; `localize` found the","-  value in one pass, the generalize workers took several hypotheses to find `run_for_time:false`.","-- **Probing synonyms instead of deriving.** D3 lost ~1.5 h and two fields hit the 6-wrong cap on `if defined`. Apply the naming laws first; `hctf labels` seeds candidates from lib/playbook.py.","-- **Per-set POST is all-or-nothing.** One wrong field fails the whole batch; `--from-solver` bisects and prints the rejected id(s). Probe uncertain label fields ONE per submit; the wrong cap is per field.","-- **Generic ATT&CK guesses** (d1 collection, d2 launcher/stager/dropper): use the role->ATT&CK table. Adapter names (regsvr32, systemd_descriptor) do NOT change the technique.","-  Exception: a plan that states `attack=` (v=3) is authoritative even when it is a parent id (T1059, T1053).","-- **Routing by file extension** (D8-D9): `.js` held HTA/WSF/SCT markup, `.vbs` a WSF job. Route by the plan marker first","-  (why the D8 solver ran unchanged through D15).","-- **Answer-id field parsing** (D8, 6 ids lost on the 1st submit): new family names contain hyphens","-  (`bash-advanced-associative-arrays-feature`, `polyglot-php-persistence-descriptor-stage-profile`). Resolve the field","-  as the longest known `-<field>` suffix (`stage-count`/`stage-profile` before `stage`), not by a prefix-strip regex.","-- **GM error body saved as the artifact** (D7 TT 26b7da83): `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` (24 B) landed as `evidence.zip`.","-  Check size + sha256 against the start response / `[assigned-artifact-sha256:..]` first; a tiny `{\"error\":..}` JSON =","-  transport failure (re-download, exit non-zero), NOT a variant -- never harvest it as a regression case.","-- **Stale notes travel with copied solvers** (D8-D15 `solver/NOTES.md` is still the D7 copy; D15's regime fix lives only in a","-  solve.py comment). Date every VARIANT AXIS line by day + attempt id; diagnose EVERY failed attempt.","-- **Unknown codec rep name -> silent no-plan** (D7 TT: 15 ids unanswered). Fall back to material-shape readings x the","-  named transform; never let an unknown NAME stop the decode.","-- **cmd arg parsing**: `%item0%` is a variable, not `%0`+`item`. CRLF/LF mixes and `SeT` casing occur.","-- **Bash Codec key**: comma-separated multi-byte keys parsed as contiguous hex give key [0] (`lib.scripts.codec_key()`).","-  **stage_count != len(steps)** (d6): read the plan field.","-- **Timed modes are a transport race.** D2 Mastery expired (downloads ate 4-5 s of 6 s); D7 TT 13.5 s for 0.4 s of solving.","-  Fork per set (D9/D15 Mastery: 5 sets in 1.8-2.4 s) and submit all sets in one call.","-- **Same-name deliveries.** Pair Mastery files by sha256; if delivery 2 is missing, leave set 2 unanswered rather than","-  reuse set 1's members (confidently wrong 42-174 times in regression cases).","-- **Re-walking nested AES zips per question** cost ~1.3 s (903 PBKDF2 runs). Index the tree once, and don't decrypt","-  script leaves to sniff for a nested zip (keep the leaf-extension list current: still missing `.lua .mof .ts .au3","-  .applescript .proj .pl` -- speed only, solve stayed ~1-2.4 s).","-- **Never execute fixtures.** Every decode so far worked from the Codec const plus a restricted interpreter of the","-  Load/Decode bodies. Cross-check two decoders; accept a plan only if it parses as `k=v|..` with `steps` (or `feature`).","+- **Regime keyed on the wrong contract field** (D16 single, 5 incorrect probes, ~1.5 min): yesterday's fix branched on","+  `run_for_time is False`; the GM moved the single solve to the statement regime too. When a carried label table breaks on","+  byte-identical constructs, assume the GM generator changed and re-check against EVERY contract key incl. `started_at`.","+- **Diffing bytes when the regime changed** (D15 Mastery, ~5 min): tabulate (construct, GM label) per contract key at once.","+- **Big Mastery bundles vs the local runner cap** (D16: 5475 ids, 5 x exec_error at 60 s). Status/contract bodies are 3-4 MB and","+  take 5-8 s each; a 5-set bundle needs start + download + solve + chunked submit (each <= 500 answers / 512 KiB). Report it to the","+  orchestrator as a budget problem; it is not a solver bug.","+- **Probing synonyms instead of deriving.** D3 lost ~1.5 h; apply the naming laws first; `hctf labels` seeds candidates.","+- **Per-set POST is all-or-nothing.** `--from-solver` bisects and prints the rejected id(s); probe uncertain label fields ONE","+  per submit (wrong cap is per field).","+- **Generic ATT&CK guesses** (d1, d2): use the role->ATT&CK table; a v=3 `attack=` is authoritative even as a parent id; a","+  prompt's ATT&CK hint (D14 T1127.001) is not.","+- **Routing by file extension** (D8-D9 `.js` held HTA/WSF/SCT, `.vbs` a WSF job): route by the plan marker first.","+- **Answer-id field parsing** (D8, 6 ids): family names contain hyphens/underscores; resolve the field as the longest known","+  `-<field>` suffix (`stage-count`/`stage-profile` before `stage`).","+- **GM error body saved as the artifact** (D7 TT): check size + sha256 against the start response first; tiny `{\"error\":..}` =","+  transport failure (re-download, exit non-zero), never a regression case.","+- **Stale notes travel with copied solvers** (D8-D16 `solver/NOTES.md` is still the D7 copy; D15-D16 regime fixes live only in","+  solve.py comments). Date every VARIANT AXIS line by day + attempt id; diagnose EVERY failed attempt.","+- **Unknown codec rep name -> silent no-plan** (D7 TT, 15 ids): fall back to material-shape readings.","+- **cmd parsing**: `%item0%` is a variable, not `%0`+`item`; CRLF/LF mixes and `SeT` casing occur. **Bash Codec key** comma","+  lists (`lib.scripts.codec_key()`). **stage_count != len(steps)**: read the plan field.","+- **Timed modes are a transport race** (D2 Mastery expired on downloads; D7 TT 13.5 s for 0.4 s of solving; D16 TT 16.7 s for","+  1.4 s). Fork per set and submit all sets in one call.","+- **Same-name deliveries**: pair Mastery files by sha256; if delivery 2 is missing, leave set 2 unanswered.","+- **Nested AES zips**: index the tree once; don't decrypt script leaves to sniff for PK (leaf-ext list still lacks `.lua .mof","+  .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb` -- speed only).","+- **Never execute fixtures.** Decode from the Codec const / descriptor plus a restricted interpreter; accept a plan only if it","+  parses as `k=v|..` with `steps` (or `feature`)."]}],"originalFile":"# script-analysis — technique log (days 1-15; updated after every day)\n\nHow this lane has looked so far (these are observations, not guarantees):\n- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field.\n- One AES zip `evidence.zip` (password `infected`) of inert \"Huntress Script Triage\" fixtures. **The contract is CUMULATIVE**:\n  each day keeps every earlier file/question and adds one language; bytes and values re-roll daily. PS (d1, 15 ids) ->\n  +JScript (d2, 87) -> +Batch (d3, 159) -> +VBScript (d4, 231) -> +Python (d5, 357) -> +Bash (d6, 399) -> +Node `.mjs` + Bash\n  advanced (d7, 469) -> +PHP polyglot + WSF/HTA/PHP-webshell hosts (d8, 615) -> +Lua + SCT/OpenResty hosts (d9, 695) -> +WMI MOF\n  (d10, 753) -> +TypeScript (d11, 811) -> +AutoIt (d12, 855) -> +AppleScript (d13, 913) -> +MSBuild `.proj` (d14, 971) -> +4 Perl\n  `.pl` polyglot + `host-perl-cgi-perl.pl` (d15, 1026; 116 members). Most days also add 2 Bash advanced fixtures (not d12, d15).\n  The title names the new language; the prompt names its NEW roles.\n- From day 2 on, every fixture hides a **self-describing plan**: `v=N|steps=a,b|adapter=..|stage_count=..|campaign_id=..|<indicators>`. It sits behind a codec, usually named in a `Codec_<id>` / `CODEC_<id>` / `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` const of the form `rep|transform|key`. Most exact_text answers are plan values copied verbatim.\n  From D8 there is also a **`v=3` plan**: it carries `role=` and `attack=` itself, and sits behind a `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-` comment.\n- The hard part is **naming CODE SHAPE**: control-flow, expansion, and function/invocation/property styles. These are GM synthetic labels that are not in the plan. Role and scenario are enums, so read `accepted_values`.\n- Files are named by behaviour (host-context, memory-stage, embedded-write, remote-write, local-dispatch, staged-handoff/-chain, outbound-transfer, impact-plan, relay-handoff, schedule-descriptor). The answer-id is `<lang>-<role>-<field>`, and the artifact path picks the file. Don't trust the file name over the plan `steps`.\n- D8-D15 prompts are narrative (\"doesn't match its siblings\", \"impossible family tree\", \"survive a reboot\", D15 \"a store that\n  was never there\"). No question ever asked for that outlier. Answer the contract ids only.\n- Time Trial windows are about 5-13 s (30 s on d1). Mastery has `setN.` ids: 2 sets on d2-d7, **5 sets on d8 (3075 ids, 22 s)\n  and d9 (3475 ids, 30 s)**, 2 sets again on d10 (1506 ids, 32 s), d11 (1622 ids, 11 s), d12 (1710 ids, 30 s), d13 (1826 ids, 80 s) and d14 (1942 ids, 30 s); **5 sets again on d15 (5130 ids, untimed regular pool)**. The artifact was `evidence-0N.zip`, or (d6) `delivery N: evidence.zip`, or (d7-d9) ONE download\n  `evidence-01.zip` that holds every `evidence-0N.zip`. Same-named deliveries: pair them by sha256. Timed question texts\n  carry `[assigned-artifact-sha256:<hex>]` per member -- usable to verify the bytes you got.\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants of the SAME day -- parse every value listed)\nEach miss below cost one failed timed attempt + a ~45-90 s generalize cycle (D6 replay: 4 cycles; D7: 1 cycle; D8-D14: 0;\nD15: 1 TT localize + 1 Mastery cycle with 2 generalize workers, ~5 min, all from the GM-LABEL-REGIME axis below).\n- **GM label regime per pool (D15, NEW; batch `expansion`)** -- SAME bytes, SAME question text, DIFFERENT label. Single solve\n  (no `run_for_time` key) and every older D3-D14 timed case label the whole handoff: `echo(!var!)` => `delayed` unless a FOR/h-pool\n  rule fires. The D15 untimed regular pool (contract `run_for_time:false`, `variant_fresh:true`; TT 0df5072d, Mastery 7fbfc526)\n  labels the JOIN STATEMENT ALONE (54 GM labels, 0 conflicts): `!a!!b!` join = delayed; `for %%G in (..) do call set` = for_indirect\n  for ANY pool (incl. `%%h%%G%%` with an `if defined` reset -- old regime said call_double); bare `call set \"x=%%h0%%..\"` (h pool)\n  = call_double; bare `call set` over item/v_a/FrAg pools = percent; plain `set \"x=%a%%b%\"` = percent. The diff is in the\n  contract's metadata, not the bytes -- two generalize workers burned time diffing byte-identical files. Parse rule: branch\n  the label table on `contract.get(\"run_for_time\") is False`; otherwise keep the old regime. Expect other synthetic-label fields\n  (control/style) to be able to flip the same way: when byte-identical constructs get different GM labels across cases,\n  diff the CONTRACT keys (run_for_time, hall_of_fame_eligible, variant_fresh) first.\n- **Codec per file** -- rep x transform x key re-rolls per variant; never bind a role to the sample's codec. **NEW rep\n  NAMES appear only on variants** (D7 TT: `unicode_escapes` `\\u00XX..`, `json_numbers` `[232,241,..]`,\n  `reversed_base64`, Bash `xor_hex|cd`). Decode by the material's SHAPE (escapes / int array / hex / base64, each also\n  reversed) x the named transform, and accept only output starting `v=`; the name only orders the tries.\n  D9-D15: no rep/transform beyond lib.codec's D3-D8 vocabulary (0 decode failures).\n- **Codec spec arity** -- 3 fields `rep|transform|key`, 2 fields `rep|` (empty transform = identity; D7-D9 bash advanced\n  fixtures), or the transform folded into the rep with the key second (`xor_hex|cd`, D8 `xor_hex|11`, D9 `xor_hex|95/6f/c0`).\n  Split on `|`, never index blindly. lib.codec (`_spec`) normalises both short forms.\n- **Plan carrier tag (v=3, D8-D9)** -- `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-<data>`, plus the same data in `descriptor_<id> = \"..\"`.\n  Values: `B64` (base64), `HEX` (plain hex), `HB64` (hex of base64 text = 2 layers), `FRAG` (hex split by `.` every 24 chars).\n  Across every delivery D8-D15 the tag stayed fixed per file; only the values re-rolled. Parse rule: ignore the tag\n  name. Peel by shape and recurse (max 3 layers): if the text is only hex digits plus `.:,-_ |\\x%` separators, strip the\n  separators and unhex; otherwise base64 (also reversed). Accept only a result starting `v=`. The tag = `obfuscation_profile`.\n  `lib.codec.find_codecs(src)` returns the v=3 plan (tag -> rep: B64 base64_literal, HEX/FRAG hex_compact, HB64 hex_base64).\n- **Plan carrier host syntax (v=3)** -- the marker sits in whatever comment the host uses: `//` (PHP, JS, HTA, WSF, SCT CDATA,\n  MOF, TS), `--` (Lua D9, AppleScript D13), `;` (AutoIt, D12), `<!-- -->` (MSBuild XML, D14), `#` (Perl, D15), and the descriptor as `$descriptor_<id>`, `var descriptor_<id>`, `local\n  descriptor_<id>`, `Global Const $descriptor_<id> = \"..\"` (AutoIt), `property descriptor_<id> : \"..\"` (AppleScript), an XML property element `<PropertyGroup><HuntressDescriptor>..</HuntressDescriptor>`\n  (MSBuild, D14 -- no `descriptor_` name at all), `my $descriptor_<id> = \"..\";` (Perl, D15). Parse rule: regex\n  `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V\\d+\\s*:\\s*(\\w*)-?\\s*([^\\s\"'<>\\]]+)` over the raw bytes, independent of comment syntax and extension.\n- **Numeric literal radix** -- the same array/constant may be decimal `23,7`, hex `0x17,0x07`, or a separator-joined\n  string decoded with `parseInt(x, R)` / `int(x, R)`: READ THE RADIX FROM THE CODE, never guess it from the digits\n  (D6: JScript material array hex on TT; Mastery dash-joined DECIMALS with `parseInt(..,10)`). Applies to keys too.\n- **Base64 alphabet** -- standard and urlsafe (`-` `_`) both occur; strip/whitelist accordingly and pad (D6 Python TT).\n- **Reversal level** -- `reversed_hex/_decimal/_integer_list` reverse the loaded LIST; `reversed_base64` reverses the\n  TEXT before decoding (`==Adu..`). Try both orders.\n- **Carrier of the same language** -- plain source vs a frozen executable (D6: Python plan inside a cx_Freeze build on\n  a TT variant). Locate the material by its markers (`MATERIAL_`/`CODEC_`/`v=`/`HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_`), not by file type.\n- **Material layout** -- one literal, split chunks, `+=` concatenation, adjacent quoted strings, `.`-separated FRAG\n  fragments; join before decoding.\n- **Adapter values** re-roll within a role (Node stager http_then_module/https_then_vm/fetch_then_function; launcher\n  execfile_node/fork_module/spawn_file; persistence systemd_descriptor/npm_lifecycle_descriptor) -- always plan-verbatim.\n- **No-new-axis days** (bytes): D8-D14 and D15 (TT 0df5072d, Mastery 7fbfc526; the 4 `.pl` + perl_cgi host kept tags/steps/\n  next_language in all 6 deliveries). Structure, tags, role/attack/steps/profiles identical to the single; only values\n  re-rolled. D8-D14 all CORRECT first try; D15's only misses came from the label-regime axis above.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n| You see | First move |\n|---|---|\n| `evidence.zip`, \"method=AES Encrypted\" | Already extracted by triage (`work/extracted/`, password `infected`) and every plan decoded in triage.md -- start from that, BUT diff the extracted member list against the contract's `artifact` names. **Triage silently skips each day's new extension**: D7 `.mjs`, D8 `.php` (HB64 peeled 1 layer only), D9 `.lua` (5 files, no decode lines). In solve.py open members with `lib.common.read_member` (Python zipfile cannot read AES). Mastery may be a zip inside a zip; walk it once. |\n| Prior-day languages in the contract | Cumulative: derive every family from TODAY's bytes with the shared codec method below. Spend thinking on the new language. If yesterday's solver routes by plan MARKER (not extension) it may already cover today (D9: unchanged D8 solver, 695/695). |\n| `.ps1` with `$encodedMaterial = [Convert]::FromBase64String('..')` + `$reconstruct` + `$nativeTypes` | `base64 -d` -> JSON descriptor (short keys a/b/c..): url/wallet/mutex/UA/file/ext/note. Match indicators by SHAPE, not key. `$nativeTypes` gives the scenario: Process/Registry+wallet=resource, ZipFile/HttpWebRequest=collection, Aes/DirectoryInfo=impact. |\n| `.js` WSH, `decode_*`/`recover_*`/`inspect_*`, XOR key arrays, `\"52:90:..\"` strings | Run each file in an empty `node` `vm` context (no require/ActiveXObject), `eval` swapped for a capture. Call the top-level functions and keep the first object that has `steps`. Read the styles off the `inspect_*` body. |\n| Timed contract with `run_for_time: false` / `variant_fresh: true` | Untimed regular pool (D15): batch `expansion` uses the statement-only label table (Variant axes). Check this key before trusting labels harvested from the single or from older timed cases. |\n| `.bat/.cmd` with `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` / `HUNTRESS-MATERIAL:`, `set \"itemN=v=1|steps=..`, `:HUNTRESS_INSPECT` | Plan is in plain `set` fragments. Emulate cmd expansion in Python (`%v%`, `!v!`, `call set %%..%%`, `for %%G in (..)`). The MATERIAL line is a 2nd encoded copy to cross-check. Never run cmd. |\n| `.vbs` with `Const Material_<id>`, `Const Codec_<id> = \"rep|transform|key\"`, `Load_/Decode_/Recover_<id>` | Decode in Python from the Codec const, cross-check against the Load/Decode code (no cscript). rep/transform answers = Codec fields 1/2 verbatim. Control = the construct wrapping the `Decode_` call inside `Recover_`. |\n| `.py` `*-recovered.py` with `MATERIAL_<id>`, `CODEC_<id>`, `load_/decode_/surface_/plan_<id>` | Already-recovered source (no decompile on d5). Decode from CODEC or run `decode_(load_(MATERIAL))` under an AST whitelist. Plan v=2 carries syntax/obfuscation/carrier/windows_chain verbatim. |\n| `.sh` `readonly Material_<id>='..'` + `readonly Codec_<id>='rep|transform|key'` | Decode from the Codec const (key hex; multi-byte key = COMMA list). Re-join split/`+=`/adjacent-quoted chunks. Never run bash. |\n| `.sh` with `Feature_<id>()` (`${!pointer}`, `local -a parts=('cu' 'rl')`, `local -A`, `${arr[@]:1:2}`, `trap 'return 0' RETURN`, a self-calling `walk_fixture`), plan `v=1|feature=..|primitive=..` | Role `advanced_syntax` (closed enum value). feature/primitive/campaign/stage_count/steps are plan-verbatim; attack = T1059.004. The `Feature_` body is the feature; never name it from the code, copy the plan. |\n| `.mjs` ESM: `const Material_<id> = \"..\"; const Codec_<id> = \"rep|transform|key\"`, async `load_/decode_/recover_/inspect_/plan_<id>`, `process.env.HUNTRESS_INSPECT_ONLY` | Static decode with `lib.codec.find_codecs` + shape fallback (reps hex_buffer, hex_array, escaped_octets `\\\\xNN`, decimal_array, unicode_escapes, json_numbers). Don't run it (top-level await, Buffer/vm). Plan fields verbatim; role from `steps`. |\n| `// HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG>-..` or `-- HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:..` + `descriptor_<id> = \"..\"` (`.php`; `.lua` `local descriptor_..` + `build_plan_<id>`, OpenResty `inert_handler_<id>` returning `{status=200,..}`; `.js` that is really HTA `<hta:application>`, WSF `<job><script language=\"JScript\">` or SCT `<?xml?><scriptlet><registration progid=..>` CDATA; `.vbs` that is a WSF job; `.au3` AutoIt `; HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:` + `Global Const $descriptor_..`; `.proj` MSBuild `<!-- HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:..-->` + `<HuntressDescriptor>`; `.pl` Perl `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:` + `use strict;` + `my $descriptor_..`) | **Route by the marker, before the extension** (the extension lies). Peel the descriptor by shape to `v=3|language=..|role=..|verdict=..|attack=..|adapter=..|host_profile=..|obfuscation_profile=..|stage_profile=..|next_language=..|stage_count=..|steps=..|campaign_id=..|url=..|file_path=..`. EVERY answer, including role and attack, is plan-verbatim. Python `-I` + base64/bytes.fromhex is enough. |\n| Real `.pyc` / PyInstaller / pyarmor (not seen yet) | `lib.pyc.recover_python(path)` (pyinstxtractor-ng + decompyle3, `dis` fallback). See skills/script-analysis. |\n| Any `Codec_` key like `ba` / `0a` | A hex byte, not text. Transforms are named for the ENCODE side: `subtract_modulo_256` decodes by ADDING, `add_modulo_256` by SUBTRACTING. `rolling_xor` = c ^ previous CIPHER byte, seeded with the key. |\n\n## Codec table (`Codec_<id>='<rep>|<transform>|<key>'`, batch `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:<rep>|<transform>`; seen D3-D9)\n**Already done for you:** triage.md's \"Decoded payloads\" runs `lib.codec` on every declared codec (and a node vm\nsandbox on JScript). In solve.py call `lib.codec.find_codecs(text)` / `lib.codec.decode(material, rep, transform, key)`\n(pure Python, Homebase-safe, unknown names -> None). A line `NOT decoded by lib.codec` = new rep/transform/arity: decode\nit by material shape yourself and list it under `## Proposed lib additions` in NOTES.md. D9 added nothing new.\n- Reps (how the bytes are WRITTEN): base64_literal/_chunks, urlsafe_base64, reversed_base64 (D7); hex_pairs/_compact/\n  _colon/_dash/_escape (`\\x`)/_literal (`0x`)/_buffer/_array (`[\"69\",\"22\"]`), percent_hex (`%xx`), escaped_octets\n  (`\\\\xNN`), unicode_escapes (`\\\\u00NN`); decimal_bytes/_comma/_dash/_pipe/_dot/_colon/_space/_csv/_array, json_numbers,\n  integer_list/_tuple, octal_space; reversed_text/_hex/_decimal/_integer_list; plain_fragments/split_fragments;\n  v=3 hex_base64 (D8).\n- Transforms (ENCODE-side names; key hex, multi-byte = COMMA list): identity (also EMPTY field), reverse/reverse_bytes,\n  single_byte_xor, repeating_key_xor, reverse_then_xor, rolling_xor (2 flavours), add_modulo_256 (decode SUBTRACTS),\n  subtract_modulo_256 (decode ADDS); batch carries the parameter in the name: xor_5a, add_7 (decimal), rotate_left\n  (undo = rotate right), reverse_xor; bash `xor_hex|<key>` = hex then XOR key (D7-D9).\n- Check: the decoded plaintext starts `v=` (or `{` JSON). If not, the codec reading is wrong.\n\n## Day by day\n**D1-D7 (PS 15 -> +JScript -> +Batch -> +VBScript -> +Python -> +Bash -> +Node, 469 ids)**: D1 collection ATT&CK cost 5\nwrong before `T1555.003` (map the SPECIFIC artifact); D2 handoff = `staged_chain`, 7 wrong ATT&CK guesses; **D3 ~1 h 45 min,\n~127 rejected probes** on batch expansion/control labels -> NAMING LAWS; D4 VBS control probed one field at a time (4 wrong);\nD5-D6 0 wrong, ~4 min (plan v=2; stage_count = plan field, not len(steps)); D7 469/469 in ~100 s, TT missed 15 ids on new reps\nand one attempt saved `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` as the zip -> **diagnose EVERY failed attempt, not only the latest.**\n**D8-D14 (+PHP polyglot & 4 host formats, +Lua/SCT/OpenResty, +WMI MOF, +TypeScript, +AutoIt, +AppleScript, +MSBuild `.proj`;\n+2 Bash advanced most days; 615 -> 971 ids)**: D8 introduced the v=3 plan (`HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-` + descriptor, byte-identical;\nrole/attack/adapter/profiles stated -- **copy, don't derive**); 6 ids lost once to hyphenated family names (longest-known-suffix\nfield parse). Since then each new language = 4 polyglots (role benign_utility/downloader/launcher/staged_chain, attack\nnone/T1105/T1059/T1059, adapter local_parser/http_client/process_builder/operation_graph, obfuscation plain_hex/base64/hex_base64/\nfragmented_hex, campaign `<LANG>-<8hex>`, url `https://<lang>-<10hex>.example.invalid/stage`, file_path\n`/tmp/huntress-<lang>/.<16hex>.stage`). D14 family has an UNDERSCORE (`polyglot-msbuild_xml-..`, campaign `MSBUILD_XML-..`);\nits prompt's MSBuild ATT&CK (T1127.001) was NOT the answer, the plan said T1059. Narrative prompts (impossible family tree,\nreboot-surviving subscription, archive delivery chain, trusted toolchain) were never asked. Marker-routed solver unchanged, 0\nwrong, all modes first try (single T+11 s on D14; TT 3-7 s, mostly GM latency).\n**D15 Crumb Trail (+4 Perl `.pl` polyglot + 1 Perl host; 1026 ids, 116 members)**: prompt \"credential-access-shaped code\nrummaging through the browser's cupboards ... find the reference that points at a store that was never there\" -- flavour only;\nno credential-store/outlier question was asked (the PS collection fixture stayed T1555.003).\n- New: `polyglot-perl-{benign-utility,downloader,launcher,staged-chain}.pl` and `host-perl-cgi-perl.pl` = `#!/usr/bin/env perl` +\n  `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<HEX|B64|HB64|FRAG>-..` + `use strict; use warnings; my $descriptor_<id> = \"..\";` (same data).\n  Plan v=3 `language=perl`, campaign `PERL-<8hex>`, url `https://perl-<10hex>.example.invalid/stage`, file_path\n  `/tmp/huntress-perl/.<16hex>.stage`, host_profile `standalone` / `perl_cgi`. Every answer plan-verbatim (host perl_cgi =\n  staged_chain/T1059/operation_graph; downloader T1105; benign `none`). Triage decoded the `.pl` plans this time.\n- Single: carried-over marker-routed solver, harness race probe 1026/1026 CORRECT at T+17 s, 0 wrong.\n- TT 0df5072d (untimed regular pool): 8 batch-expansion ids `delayed` -> GM `percent`; localize fixed them, CORRECT at 39 s.\n  Mastery 7fbfc526 (5 sets, 5130 ids): ~25 expansion ids wrong in all 5 sets; 2 generalize workers found the\n  `run_for_time:false` statement-only regime (Variant axes); re-run left 1 miss (`set5.batch-chain-expansion`, h-pool FOR =\n  for_indirect, not call_double) fixed by localize; CORRECT ~5.5 min after start. Everything else first try.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- **Check `answer_format.kind` first.** `enum` gives the list (scenario, role). `mitre_attack_id` takes `T####[.###]` or literal `none` (benign_utility). `integer`/`ordered_tokens` (d6+). `exact_text` = plan value or synthetic label.\n- **Plan-verbatim fields** (copy exactly):\n  - adapter: COM ProgIDs `MSXML2.ServerXMLHTTP.6.0`, LOLBins `CertReq.exe`, batch `call`/`set`/`for`, Node\n    `console_report`/`typed_array_to_file`/`stream_pipeline`, v=3 local_parser/runtime_loader/file_writer/http_client/\n    process_builder/schedule_builder/operation_graph.\n  - indicators: campaign_id, host_id, url, file_path, upload_url, next_stage, extension, note_name, handoff_id, cron_path,\n    schedule_path, service_name. Indicator questions read \"exact X indicator\", where X is the plan key.\n  - per-language labels: batch `graph` (D9 confirmed linear/single/diamond/fan_out/fallback_retry/cross_language/\n    same_language), Python syntax/obfuscation/carrier/windows_chain, Bash feature/primitive, v=3 host_profile/\n    obfuscation_profile/stage_profile/next_language.\n  - v=3 host_profile seen: standalone, wsf_jscript, wsf_mixed, hta_jscript, php_webshell (D8), sct_scriptlet, lua_openresty\n    (D9), perl_cgi (D15). obfuscation: base64/plain_hex/hex_base64/fragmented_hex. stage_profile: single_descriptor/\n    two_stage_download_execute/three_stage_decode_write_launch/cross_language_handoff.\n  - Bash advanced feature|primitive (always plan-verbatim; 14 seen D7-D14), e.g. indirect_expansion|parameter_indirection,\n    associative_arrays|declare_associative, heredoc_reconstruction|quoted_heredoc, getopts_state|option_parser_state (D14),\n    brace_expansion|cartesian_brace_expansion (D14). Family = `bash-advanced-<file-stem>` (D7 short forms: `indirect`, `tokens`).\n  - **v=3 role and attack too.** GM accepted the plan's PARENT technique ids: `T1059` (launcher, staged_chain -- PHP, WSF,\n    HTA, SCT, Lua alike) and `T1053` (persistence_descriptor), NOT the host-language sub-technique. The role->ATT&CK table\n    below is for v=1/v=2 plans only. **v=3 role does NOT follow `steps`** (D14 MSBuild: benign_utility had steps\n    `decode_embedded>write_file>dispatch_process`, launcher `decode_configuration>return_configuration`) -- copy role= and steps=\n    independently; never \"fix\" one from the other.\n- **Role from `steps`** (v=1/v=2 plans; v=3 states `role=`):\n\n  | steps | role |\n  |---|---|\n  | decode_configuration,return_configuration | benign_utility |\n  | acquire_remote + dispatch_memory/dispatch_pipe | stager |\n  | acquire_remote,write_file | downloader |\n  | decode_embedded,write_file | dropper |\n  | locate_local,dispatch_process | launcher |\n  | read_file/upload,transmit_remote | uploader |\n  | transform + recovery_note | impact |\n  | build_schedule,register_descriptor (Node d7) | persistence_descriptor |\n  | recognize_syntax,reconstruct_intent + plan `feature=` (Bash d7-d9) | advanced_syntax |\n  | ends in handoff_script (JS/Batch/VBS) or profile_host..dispatch_process | staged_chain |\n  | dispatch_next_stage (Python) | relay |\n\n  cron_path/service_name on a staged_chain are indicators only, NOT persistence.\n- **Role -> ATT&CK** (GM-confirmed d2-d9; `lib.scripts.role_attack(role, lang)` has the table):\n  - benign `none`; downloader and stager T1105; dropper T1140; uploader T1041; impact T1486; persistence_descriptor\n    T1053.003 (by role, whatever the adapter); advanced_syntax T1059.004.\n  - launcher/staged_chain/relay follow the HOST LANGUAGE: T1059.003 batch, .004 bash, .005 VBS, .006 python, .007\n    JScript AND Node.js (.001 PS predicted, never asked).\n  - PS scenarios: resource_hijacking T1496, synthetic_collection T1555.003, synthetic_impact T1486.\n  - REJECTED: T1218.010, T1620, T1027.009, T1005, T1560, T1119, T1074(.001); stager T1059.007; dropper T1105.\n- **Batch expansion** (closed set; mined from EVERY GM-verified D3-D6 case, 0 conflicts in 545):\n  - fragments named `h<N>` AND joined with `call set` (bare, or `for %%G in (..) do call set`) = `call_double`\n  - `for %%G in (..) do call set \"cfg=%%cfg%%%%<pool>%%G%%\"` over any OTHER pool (v_a/item/fragment/FrAg) = `for_indirect`\n  - everything else = `delayed`, INCLUDING h-pools joined with `!h0!!h1!..` (the \"h-pool = call_double\" shortcut failed).\n  - Fragment JOINER pitfall: `set \"item9=%item0%%item1%...\"` is the JOIN, not fragment 9 -- skip `set` lines whose\n    value references the other fragments (a wrong Mastery answer on D6).\n  - D13+ question text: \"Classify only the expansion form used by the descriptor reconstruction statement\" with enum\n    percent/delayed/call_double/for_indirect. In the `run_for_time:false` pool the label follows that wording literally\n    (statement-only table under Variant axes); single solve still followed the echo(!var!) rules above.\n  - REJECTED: percent_expansion, immediate, call-double, double_call.\n- **Batch control**: direct (separator lines and `:HUNTRESS_UNUSED` dead labels are NOT control), errorlevel_guard\n  (`ver >nul` + `if errorlevel 1 exit /b 1`), goto_dispatch, call_subroutine, if_guard (`if defined X`). REJECTED:\n  linear, straight_line, sequential, goto, goto_label, double_pipe, pipe, ampersand, call_label, dead_label, errorlevel,\n  opaque_branch, + ~40 \"if defined\" synonyms.\n- **VBS control**: direct, select_case, do_once, while_once, error_guard (`On Error Resume Next`..`Err.Raise`),\n  for_once. REJECTED: do_loop, do_exit, while_wend, while_loop, on_error_resume.\n- **Codec labels**: representation/transform = the codec const's fields 1/2 copied VERBATIM; spellings differ per\n  language (Python `decimal_csv`, batch `decimal_bytes|reverse_xor`): read the const, never translate.\n- **JScript styles** (closed sets in the question text; GM-confirmed D2-D9):\n  - function-style: `function f(` = declaration; `var f = function(` = anonymous_expression; `var f = function f_body(` = named_expression.\n  - invocation-style: how recover/inspect invokes the next top-level function: `f(x)` = direct, `f.call(..)` (also via\n    a local `invoke` helper doing `block.call`) = call, `f.apply(..)` = apply.\n  - property-style: only `o.k` = dot, only `o[\"k\"]` = bracket_literal, both = mixed. triage's `shape:` line counts them.\n- **NAMING LAWS** (proven on if_guard, error_guard, do_once, pe_cli). Compose unknown labels from the SHORT language keyword:\n  - conditional/bail-out = `<keyword>_guard`; run-once loop = `<keyword>_once`; control transfer = `<keyword>_<action>`.\n  - The spelled-out statement (if_defined, on_error_resume, do_exit, while_wend) and descriptive synonyms (flag_guard, defined_guard, opaque_predicate) have ALWAYS been rejected.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **Diffing bytes when the regime changed** (D15 Mastery, ~5 min): 25 batch-expansion ids flipped delayed->percent on\n  byte-identical files. Tabulate (join shape, pool, GM label) per contract metadata key at once; `localize` found the\n  value in one pass, the generalize workers took several hypotheses to find `run_for_time:false`.\n- **Probing synonyms instead of deriving.** D3 lost ~1.5 h and two fields hit the 6-wrong cap on `if defined`. Apply the naming laws first; `hctf labels` seeds candidates from lib/playbook.py.\n- **Per-set POST is all-or-nothing.** One wrong field fails the whole batch; `--from-solver` bisects and prints the rejected id(s). Probe uncertain label fields ONE per submit; the wrong cap is per field.\n- **Generic ATT&CK guesses** (d1 collection, d2 launcher/stager/dropper): use the role->ATT&CK table. Adapter names (regsvr32, systemd_descriptor) do NOT change the technique.\n  Exception: a plan that states `attack=` (v=3) is authoritative even when it is a parent id (T1059, T1053).\n- **Routing by file extension** (D8-D9): `.js` held HTA/WSF/SCT markup, `.vbs` a WSF job. Route by the plan marker first\n  (why the D8 solver ran unchanged through D15).\n- **Answer-id field parsing** (D8, 6 ids lost on the 1st submit): new family names contain hyphens\n  (`bash-advanced-associative-arrays-feature`, `polyglot-php-persistence-descriptor-stage-profile`). Resolve the field\n  as the longest known `-<field>` suffix (`stage-count`/`stage-profile` before `stage`), not by a prefix-strip regex.\n- **GM error body saved as the artifact** (D7 TT 26b7da83): `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` (24 B) landed as `evidence.zip`.\n  Check size + sha256 against the start response / `[assigned-artifact-sha256:..]` first; a tiny `{\"error\":..}` JSON =\n  transport failure (re-download, exit non-zero), NOT a variant -- never harvest it as a regression case.\n- **Stale notes travel with copied solvers** (D8-D15 `solver/NOTES.md` is still the D7 copy; D15's regime fix lives only in a\n  solve.py comment). Date every VARIANT AXIS line by day + attempt id; diagnose EVERY failed attempt.\n- **Unknown codec rep name -> silent no-plan** (D7 TT: 15 ids unanswered). Fall back to material-shape readings x the\n  named transform; never let an unknown NAME stop the decode.\n- **cmd arg parsing**: `%item0%` is a variable, not `%0`+`item`. CRLF/LF mixes and `SeT` casing occur.\n- **Bash Codec key**: comma-separated multi-byte keys parsed as contiguous hex give key [0] (`lib.scripts.codec_key()`).\n  **stage_count != len(steps)** (d6): read the plan field.\n- **Timed modes are a transport race.** D2 Mastery expired (downloads ate 4-5 s of 6 s); D7 TT 13.5 s for 0.4 s of solving.\n  Fork per set (D9/D15 Mastery: 5 sets in 1.8-2.4 s) and submit all sets in one call.\n- **Same-name deliveries.** Pair Mastery files by sha256; if delivery 2 is missing, leave set 2 unanswered rather than\n  reuse set 1's members (confidently wrong 42-174 times in regression cases).\n- **Re-walking nested AES zips per question** cost ~1.3 s (903 PBKDF2 runs). Index the tree once, and don't decrypt\n  script leaves to sniff for a nested zip (keep the leaf-extension list current: still missing `.lua .mof .ts .au3\n  .applescript .proj .pl` -- speed only, solve stayed ~1-2.4 s).\n- **Never execute fixtures.** Every decode so far worked from the Codec const plus a restricted interpreter of the\n  Load/Decode bodies. Cross-check two decoders; accept a plan only if it parses as `k=v|..` with `steps` (or `feature`).\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Hvt5Ae8vnXrnhq5RNs5fXd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
