. Move it into a prebuilt function label_expansion(join_stmt, pool, contract) with both tables and GM-verified fixtures (D3-D14 cases old regime; D15 TT 0df5072d/Mastery 7fbfc526 and D16 single 89161077/TT a719c002 statement regime: !a!!b! delayed, for..call set for_indirect, bare call set h-pool call_double, bare call set other pools / plain %a%%b% percent). Same switch hook for batch control and VBS control in case they flip next.\"),\n G(\"v3-next-lang-fixture-battery\",\"regression fixtures for the next likely v=3 hosts\",1,\"prebuild\",\n   \"Synthetic inert fixtures x 4 tags (B64/HEX/HB64/FRAG) for: PowerShell .psm1 (marker inside <# #>, `$descriptor_x = @'..'@` here-string), Tcl (`set descriptor_x {..}`), Go (`descriptor_x := `..``), Groovy/Jenkinsfile (`def descriptor_x = '''..'''`), Kotlin .kts (`val`), R (`<-`), GH Actions YAML (`descriptor_x: |` block scalar), Dockerfile (`ARG DESCRIPTOR_X=`), Makefile (`DESCRIPTOR_X := ` + `\\\\` continuation), XSLT (`<msxsl:script>` CDATA), .reg (UTF-16LE). Gate: the carried solve.py v=3 path returns the plan for every one. Ruby (D16) and Perl (D15) passed unchanged -- keep proving the next ones before they drop.\"),\n G(\"mastery-runner-budget\",\"5-set Mastery bundles exceed the 60 s local hb_timed cap\",1,\"note\",\n   \"D16 Mastery (5475 ids, 3.2-3.7 MB contract/status bodies at 5-8 s each) ended exec_error 'local hb_timed timed out' on 5/5 attempts, nothing submitted. Orchestrator item (hctf/workers.py run_timed timeout=60), not a lane module: raise the cap for untimed run_for_time:false pools or stream start->download->solve->chunked submit. Lane side: keep solve under ~3 s (fork per set).\"),\n G(\"wsh-script-encoder-decode\",\"JScript.Encode / VBScript.Encode (#@~^..^#~@) in pure Python\",2,\"prebuild\",\n   \"Cheap mutation of the carried .js/.vbs/WSF/HTA/SCT hosts (`language=\\\"JScript.Encode\\\"`, .jse/.vbe). Pure-python decoder (the 3 permutation tables + checksum) -> then normal routing. Oracle: .venv/bin/wshenc.\"),\n G(\"ruby-perl-pack-reps\",\"pack/unpack-style codec reps of the Unix scripting languages\",2,\"prebuild\",\n   \"If v=1-style Codec_ fixtures come to Perl/Ruby/Tcl: `[\\\"..\\\"].pack(\\\"H*\\\")`, `.unpack1(\\\"m0\\\")`/`unpack(\\\"m\\\")`, `pack(\\\"C*\\\", ..)`, `\\\\u{..}`/`\\\\x{..}` escapes, `%w[..]` word arrays, Perl `pack(\\\"H*\\\", ..)`/`MIME::Base64::decode`, Tcl `binary decode hex|base64`, Lua `\\\\ddd`. Add as lib.codec-compatible readings keyed by material shape + named template.\"),\n G(\"yaml-ci-host-route\",\"GitHub Actions / GitLab CI / Ansible YAML host\",2,\"prebuild\",\n   \"Supply-chain / trusted-toolchain host fits the D14 MSBuild + D15/D16 web-host direction. yaml.safe_load (installed) walk of every string; marker in `#` comments (not in the parsed tree -> also regex raw text); descriptor as a key or `|`/`>` block scalar (strip indentation, join folded lines). Family likely `host-github_actions-<lang>` (underscore).\"),\n G(\"python-exec-onion-static\",\"exec(marshal/zlib/base64(..)) / lambda onions without exec\",2,\"prebuild\",\n   \"AST walker that folds b64decode/b85decode/zlib.decompress/bytes.fromhex/[::-1]/codecs.decode(rot13) calls on literals and stops at exec/eval/marshal.loads; marshal blobs -> xdis disassembly (version from magic) to pull const strings. Replaces the old python-exec-layers note; Python is the only carried language with a carrier axis (D6 cx_Freeze).\"),\n G(\"reg-inf-host-route\",\".reg / .inf persistence hosts\",2,\"prebuild\",\n   \".reg = UTF-16LE + BOM; values `hex(2):`/`hex(7):` are comma-hex of UTF-16LE text, `\\\\` line continuations; .inf [Strings] %var% substitution, RunPreSetupCommands / UnRegisterOCXSection. Decode every value to text, then plan-scan. Builds on source-encoding-normalize.\"),\n G(\"vba-module-route\",\"VBA modules (.bas/.cls, vbaProject.bin MS-OVBA compressed source)\",2,\"prebuild\",\n   \"4th WSH-family language never polyglotted. Check what container-carrier-extract emits for vbaProject.bin; add pure-python MS-OVBA decompression (dir stream -> module offsets) if missing, then Codec_/marker scan. Oracle: .venv/bin/olevba --decode.\"),\n G(\"dockerfile-makefile-route\",\"Dockerfile / Makefile build hosts\",3,\"prebuild\",\n   \"Join `\\\\` continuations; Dockerfile `ARG/ENV DESCRIPTOR_X=..`, `RUN echo .. | base64 -d | sh`; Makefile `DESCRIPTOR_X := ..`, TAB recipes, `$(shell ..)` (never `make -n`). Marker in `#` comments.\"),\n]\nkeep=[\"php-cli\",\"lua-unluac\",\"xsltproc-cabextract-yq\",\"tcl-r-interpreters\",\"applescript-scpt\",\"js-deob-extras\",\"ps-deob-modules\",\"xlm-standalone\",\"dotnet-script\"]\nnew+= [old[k] for k in keep]\nlf=old[\"leaf-ext-list\"]; lf[\"detail\"]=lf[\"detail\"].replace(\".proj .pl (and future .rb\",\".proj .pl .rb (and future\")\nnsl=old[\"new-synthetic-label-family\"]; nsl[\"detail\"]=\"Polyglot days have been plan-verbatim since D8, but an 'advanced <lang>' set (like bash-advanced) would bring feature/primitive or control/style labels, and OLD label families can flip regime (batch expansion D15/D16). Apply playbook NAMING LAWS; probe one field per submit; check started_at/run_for_time first.\"\nnew+=[lf,nsl,old[\"family-name-underscore\"]]\nbody=\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in new)+\"\\n]\\n\"\njson.loads(body)\ns=s[:i]+body+s[j:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(len(new), sum(1 for g in new if g[\"action\"]==\"prebuild\"))\nEOF\ntail -5 $F | cut -c1-120; wc -l $F reference/techniques/script-analysis.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":950,"cache_read_input_tokens":115503,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":950},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,